var tipuesearch = {"pages":[{"title":" fformat ","text":"fformat A formatter for free-form Fortran. The source is split into tokens ( ffmt_lexer ), grouped into\nstatements ( ffmt_statements ), classified by their role in the block structure\n( ffmt_constructs ) and analyzed for nesting depth ( ffmt_structure ). Developer Info Jacob Williams","tags":"home","url":"index.html"},{"title":"case_marks_t – fformat ","text":"type, public :: case_marks_t The letter case wanted for each token ( CASE_KEEP , CASE_LOWER or CASE_UPPER ). Inherited by type~~case_marks_t~~InheritedByGraph type~case_marks_t case_marks_t type~writer_t writer_t type~writer_t->type~case_marks_t cases Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, allocatable :: part (:) for the kind part of a token only (see kind_part ), applied\nafter whole integer, public, allocatable :: whole (:) for the whole text of each token Source Code type , public :: case_marks_t !! The letter case wanted for each token (`CASE_KEEP`, `CASE_LOWER` or `CASE_UPPER`). integer , allocatable :: whole (:) !! for the whole text of each token integer , allocatable :: part (:) !! for the kind part of a token only (see [[kind_part]]), applied !! after `whole` end type case_marks_t","tags":"","url":"type/case_marks_t.html"},{"title":"lexer_t – fformat ","text":"type, private :: lexer_t Lexer state for one source text. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial logical, public :: glue_next = .false. the next code token continues the previous one logical, public :: glue_pending = .false. the previous line ended with a code character directly followed by & integer, public :: line = 1 current line logical, public :: line_start = .true. only blanks so far on the current line Source Code type :: lexer_t !! Lexer state for one source text. integer :: line = 1 !! current line logical :: line_start = . true . !! only blanks so far on the current line logical :: glue_pending = . false . !! the previous line ended with a code character directly followed by `&` logical :: glue_next = . false . !! the next code token continues the previous one end type lexer_t","tags":"","url":"type/lexer_t.html"},{"title":"case_options_t – fformat ","text":"type, public :: case_options_t Letter case of keywords, dot operators and logical constants, intrinsic procedures, the constants\nof the intrinsic modules, and kinds. Inherited by type~~case_options_t~~InheritedByGraph type~case_options_t case_options_t type~format_options_t format_options_t type~format_options_t->type~case_options_t letter_case Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public :: constants = CASE_KEEP constants and types of iso_fortran_env and iso_c_binding : output_unit , int64 , c_int , c_ptr integer, public :: keywords = CASE_KEEP if , end do , integer , intent(in) , ... integer, public :: operators = CASE_KEEP .and. , .eq. , .true. , ... integer, public :: procedures = CASE_KEEP intrinsic procedures where they are called: size(a) , call cpu_time(t) integer, public :: types = CASE_KEEP suffixes 2_int64 and prefixes ck_'a' , exponent letters 1.0e-3 Source Code type , public :: case_options_t !! Letter case of keywords, dot operators and logical constants, intrinsic procedures, the constants !! of the intrinsic modules, and kinds. integer :: keywords = CASE_KEEP !! `if`, `end do`, `integer`, `intent(in)`, ... integer :: operators = CASE_KEEP !! `.and.`, `.eq.`, `.true.`, ... integer :: procedures = CASE_KEEP !! intrinsic procedures where they are called: `size(a)`, `call cpu_time(t)` integer :: constants = CASE_KEEP !! constants and types of `iso_fortran_env` and `iso_c_binding`: !! `output_unit`, `int64`, `c_int`, `c_ptr` integer :: types = CASE_KEEP !! kinds: `kind=` values and `real(dp)` in declarations, literal kind !! suffixes `2_int64` and prefixes `ck_'a'`, exponent letters `1.0e-3` end type case_options_t","tags":"","url":"type/case_options_t.html"},{"title":"format_options_t – fformat ","text":"type, public :: format_options_t All options that control formatting. The defaults give 4-space indentation with the bodies\nof modules and programs not indented, and aligned continuation lines. Inherits type~~format_options_t~~InheritsGraph type~format_options_t format_options_t type~case_options_t case_options_t type~format_options_t->type~case_options_t letter_case type~whitespace_options_t whitespace_options_t type~format_options_t->type~whitespace_options_t spaces Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public :: base_indent = 0 columns added to the indentation of every line, so that even\nprogram units are indented (4 for code that starts in column 5) integer, public :: comment_spacing = -1 blanks before a trailing comment, or -1 to keep them; comments\naligned with one on the line before or after are kept integer, public :: continuation = CONT_ALIGN layout of continuation lines ( CONT_ALIGN or CONT_INDENT ) integer, public :: continuation_indent = 4 extra indentation of continuation lines, used with CONT_INDENT and when there is nothing to align with integer, public :: indent = 4 spaces per indentation level logical, public :: indent_comments = .true. re-indent comment lines like the code around them logical, public :: indent_fypp = .false. indent the code inside fypp blocks ( #:if , #:for , #:def , ...),\nand the fypp directive lines with the code around them logical, public :: indent_procedures = .true. indent the bodies of subroutines and functions logical, public :: indent_units = .false. indent the bodies of modules, submodules and main programs logical, public :: keep_column1_comments = .false. leave comment lines that start in column 1 there (with indent_comments ) type( case_options_t ), public :: letter_case letter case of keywords and operators integer, public :: line_length = 132 maximum line length (0 for no limit). Alignment that would make a\nline longer falls back to a smaller indentation. integer, public :: relational = REL_KEEP spelling of relational operators: REL_KEEP , REL_SYMBOLS ( .lt. becomes < ) or REL_LETTERS ( < becomes .lt. ) logical, public :: sort_use = .false. sort the use statements of each group by module name logical, public :: sort_use_only = .false. sort the names in only: lists type( whitespace_options_t ), public :: spaces whitespace rules within lines logical, public :: split_lines = .true. split code lines that are longer than line_length Source Code type , public :: format_options_t !! All options that control formatting. The defaults give 4-space indentation with the bodies !! of modules and programs not indented, and aligned continuation lines. integer :: indent = 4 !! spaces per indentation level integer :: base_indent = 0 !! columns added to the indentation of every line, so that even !! program units are indented (4 for code that starts in column 5) logical :: indent_units = . false . !! indent the bodies of modules, submodules and main programs logical :: indent_procedures = . true . !! indent the bodies of subroutines and functions logical :: indent_fypp = . false . !! indent the code inside fypp blocks (`#:if`, `#:for`, `#:def`, ...), !! and the fypp directive lines with the code around them integer :: continuation = CONT_ALIGN !! layout of continuation lines (`CONT_ALIGN` or `CONT_INDENT`) integer :: continuation_indent = 4 !! extra indentation of continuation lines, used with `CONT_INDENT` !! and when there is nothing to align with logical :: indent_comments = . true . !! re-indent comment lines like the code around them logical :: keep_column1_comments = . false . !! leave comment lines that start in column 1 there (with !! `indent_comments`) integer :: line_length = 132 !! maximum line length (0 for no limit). Alignment that would make a !! line longer falls back to a smaller indentation. logical :: split_lines = . true . !! split code lines that are longer than `line_length` integer :: relational = REL_KEEP !! spelling of relational operators: `REL_KEEP`, `REL_SYMBOLS` !! (`.lt.` becomes `<`) or `REL_LETTERS` (`<` becomes `.lt.`) logical :: sort_use = . false . !! sort the `use` statements of each group by module name logical :: sort_use_only = . false . !! sort the names in `only:` lists integer :: comment_spacing = - 1 !! blanks before a trailing comment, or -1 to keep them; comments !! aligned with one on the line before or after are kept type ( whitespace_options_t ) :: spaces !! whitespace rules within lines type ( case_options_t ) :: letter_case !! letter case of keywords and operators end type format_options_t","tags":"","url":"type/format_options_t.html"},{"title":"whitespace_options_t – fformat ","text":"type, public :: whitespace_options_t Modes of the whitespace rules. The defaults follow the most common style in practice where it is\nclear-cut, and keep the rest. Inherited by type~~whitespace_options_t~~InheritedByGraph type~whitespace_options_t whitespace_options_t type~format_options_t format_options_t type~format_options_t->type~whitespace_options_t spaces Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public :: assignment = WS_ADD = outside brackets: assignments, initializations, do i = 1, n integer, public :: comma = WS_KEEP , : with WS_ADD , no blank before and at least one after integer, public :: concat = WS_REMOVE // integer, public :: conditional = WS_ADD ? and : of a conditional expression (c ? a : b) (F2023) integer, public :: control_paren = WS_ADD between if , while , select case , where , ... and ( , and\nbetween ) and a final then integer, public :: declarations = WS_ADD :: integer, public :: defined_operators = WS_KEEP binary user-defined operators: a .plus. b integer, public :: keyword_args = WS_REMOVE = inside brackets: f(x=1) , intent= , len=* integer, public :: logical = WS_KEEP .and. .or. .eqv. .neqv. integer, public :: mult_div = WS_KEEP binary * / integer, public :: percent = WS_REMOVE % integer, public :: plus_minus = WS_KEEP binary + - integer, public :: pointer = WS_ADD => : pointer assignment, renames, associate integer, public :: power = WS_REMOVE ** integer, public :: relational = WS_KEEP == /= < <= > >= and .eq. etc. integer, public :: slice_colon = WS_REMOVE : inside brackets: a(1:n) Source Code type , public :: whitespace_options_t !! Modes of the whitespace rules. The defaults follow the most common style in practice where it is !! clear-cut, and keep the rest. integer :: assignment = WS_ADD !! `=` outside brackets: assignments, initializations, `do i = 1, n` integer :: keyword_args = WS_REMOVE !! `=` inside brackets: `f(x=1)`, `intent=`, `len=*` integer :: pointer = WS_ADD !! `=>`: pointer assignment, renames, `associate` integer :: declarations = WS_ADD !! `::` integer :: relational = WS_KEEP !! `== /= < <= > >=` and `.eq.` etc. integer :: logical = WS_KEEP !! `.and. .or. .eqv. .neqv.` integer :: plus_minus = WS_KEEP !! binary `+ -` integer :: mult_div = WS_KEEP !! binary `* /` integer :: power = WS_REMOVE !! `**` integer :: concat = WS_REMOVE !! `//` integer :: comma = WS_KEEP !! `,`: with `WS_ADD`, no blank before and at least one after integer :: slice_colon = WS_REMOVE !! `:` inside brackets: `a(1:n)` integer :: percent = WS_REMOVE !! `%` integer :: control_paren = WS_ADD !! between `if`, `while`, `select case`, `where`, ... and `(`, and !! between `)` and a final `then` integer :: conditional = WS_ADD !! `?` and `:` of a conditional expression `(c ? a : b)` (F2023) integer :: defined_operators = WS_KEEP !! binary user-defined operators: `a .plus. b` end type whitespace_options_t","tags":"","url":"type/whitespace_options_t.html"},{"title":"diagnostic_t – fformat ","text":"type, public :: diagnostic_t A problem with the block structure, such as an end that matches no open construct. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public :: line = 0 source line of the statement concerned character(len=:), public, allocatable :: message what is wrong, e.g. 'if is not closed' Source Code type , public :: diagnostic_t !! A problem with the block structure, such as an `end` that matches no open construct. integer :: line = 0 !! source line of the statement concerned character ( len = :), allocatable :: message !! what is wrong, e.g. `'if is not closed'` end type diagnostic_t","tags":"","url":"type/diagnostic_t.html"},{"title":"saved_stack_t – fformat ","text":"type, private :: saved_stack_t Scope stacks for one preprocessor conditional: as it was at the #if (restored at each #elif / #else ) and as it was at the end of the first branch (used after #endif ). Inherits type~~saved_stack_t~~InheritsGraph type~