ponents, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( string_t ), public, allocatable :: exclude (:) files.exclude , likewise type( string_t ), public, allocatable :: extensions (:) files.extensions ; not allocated if the file does not set it character(len=:), public, allocatable :: path the file, or '' if there is none type( setting_t ), public, allocatable :: settings (:) the formatting settings, in the order they are applied Source Code type , public :: config_t !! The settings of one configuration file. character ( len = :), allocatable :: path !! the file, or `''` if there is none type ( setting_t ), allocatable :: settings (:) !! the formatting settings, in the order they are applied type ( string_t ), allocatable :: extensions (:) !! `files.extensions`; not allocated if the file does not set it type ( string_t ), allocatable :: exclude (:) !! `files.exclude`, likewise end type config_t","tags":"","url":"type/config_t.html"},{"title":"piece_t – fformat ","text":"type, private :: piece_t A piece of an output line: a token, or the blanks before one. Its text is src(first:last) (with the token's letter case applied), or blanks blanks if that is positive; it is not\ncopied, so that measuring a line allocates nothing. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public :: blanks = 0 if positive, the piece is this many blanks instead integer, public :: first = 1 first byte of the text in the source integer, public :: last = 0 last byte of the text in the source integer, public :: tok = 0 token index, or 0 for blanks Source Code type :: piece_t !! A piece of an output line: a token, or the blanks before one. Its text is `src(first:last)` !! (with the token's letter case applied), or `blanks` blanks if that is positive; it is not !! copied, so that measuring a line allocates nothing. integer :: tok = 0 !! token index, or 0 for blanks integer :: first = 1 !! first byte of the text in the source integer :: last = 0 !! last byte of the text in the source integer :: blanks = 0 !! if positive, the piece is this many blanks instead end type piece_t","tags":"","url":"type/piece_t.html"},{"title":"writer_t – fformat ","text":"type, private :: writer_t Output being built, and the alignment state of the current statement. Inherits type~~writer_t~~InheritsGraph type~writer_t writer_t type~case_marks_t case_marks_t type~writer_t->type~case_marks_t cases type~string_builder_t string_builder_t type~writer_t->type~string_builder_t buf Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public :: anchor_col (3) = -1 column of the first item after an assignment = / => ,\na use statement's only: and a declaration's :: , or -1 integer, public, allocatable :: bracket_first (:) column of the first item after each open bracket, or -1;\nonly bracket_first(1:nbrackets) is in use type( string_builder_t ), public :: buf the output text type( case_marks_t ), public :: cases letter case wanted for each token (see compute_case ) integer, public :: col = 0 output column: characters since the last line break integer, public :: comment_in = -1 input column of the comment on the previous line, or -1 integer, public :: comment_out = -1 output column of that comment logical, public :: declaration = .false. a top-level :: has been seen in the current statement integer, public, allocatable :: gap (:) blanks wanted before each token (see compute_gaps ) logical, public :: generic = .false. the current statement is a generic binding logical, public :: keep_original = .true. fall back to a code line's original indentation when the\nnew one