t. Outside\nthe statement only '' matches. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( statement_view_t ), intent(in) :: v the statement integer, intent(in) :: j index into v%code(:) character(len=*), intent(in) :: text the text, in lowercase Return Value logical procedure, public :: kind_of => view_kind_of kind of a code token private pure function view_kind_of (v, j) result(kind) Kind ( TK_* ) of code token j , or 0 outside the statement. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( statement_view_t ), intent(in) :: v the statement integer, intent(in) :: j index into v%code(:) Return Value integer procedure, public :: word => view_word lowercase text of a code token private pure function view_word (v, j) result(w) Lowercase text of code token j , or '' outside the statement. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( statement_view_t ), intent(in) :: v the statement integer, intent(in) :: j index into v%code(:) Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Source Code type , public :: statement_view_t !! The code tokens of one statement, with their lowercase text and bracket depth: what the rules !! that read a statement word by word need. The procedures take an index `j` into `code(:)`; !! outside `1:n` a word is `''` and its kind 0, so a rule can look before and after a token !! without checking the bounds. integer , allocatable :: code (:) !! indices into the token list of the code tokens !! (see [[code_tokens]]) integer :: n = 0 !! number of code tokens integer :: first = 1 !! first code token after a statement label (`10 continue`) integer , allocatable :: kinds (:) !! kind of each code token (`TK_*`) integer , allocatable :: depth (:) !! open `(` and `[` around each code token; a bracket is !! outside its own pair character ( len = :), allocatable :: low !! lowercase text of the code tokens, one after another integer , allocatable :: lo (:) !! where the text of each code token starts in `low` integer , allocatable :: hi (:) !! where it ends contains procedure :: word => view_word !! lowercase text of a code token procedure :: is => view_is !! whether a code token's lowercase text is a given one procedure :: kind_of => view_kind_of !! kind of a code token procedure :: closing => view_closing !! the `)` that closes a `(` end type statement_view_t","tags":"","url":"type/statement_view_t.html"},{"title":"read_file – fformat","text":"public  subroutine read_file(path, text, stat, errmsg) All bytes of file path . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: path the file to read character(len=:), intent(out), allocatable :: text the contents; '' if the file cannot be opened integer, intent(out) :: stat iostat of the open or read: nonzero on failure character(len=:), intent(out), allocatable :: errmsg the system's message, if stat is nonzero Called by proc~~read_file~~CalledByGraph proc~read_file read_file proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~read_file proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine read_file ( path , text , stat , errmsg ) !! All bytes of file `path`. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path !! the file to read character ( len = :), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: text !! the contents; `''` if the file cannot be opened integer , intent ( out ) :: stat !! `iostat` of the open or read: nonzero on failure character ( len = :), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: errmsg !! the system's message, if `stat` is nonzero integer :: unit , nbytes character ( len = 256 ) :: msg text = '' open ( newunit = unit , file = path , access = 'stream' , form = 'unformatted' , status = 'old' , & action = 'read' , iostat = stat , iomsg = msg ) if ( stat /= 0 ) then errmsg = trim ( msg ) return end if inquire ( unit = unit , size = nbytes ) if ( nbytes > 0 ) then deallocate ( text ) allocate ( character ( len = nbytes ) :: text ) read ( unit , iostat = stat , iomsg = msg ) text if ( stat /= 0 ) errmsg = trim ( msg ) end if close ( unit ) end subroutine read_file","tags":"","url":"proc/read_file.html"},{"title":"read_stdin – fformat","text":"public  subroutine read_stdin(text) Uses iso_fortran_env ffmt_strings proc~~read_stdin~~UsesGraph proc~read_stdin read_stdin iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env proc~read_stdin->iso_fortran_env module~ffmt_strings ffmt_strings proc~read_stdin->module~ffmt_strings Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. All of standard input. Lines are read as text, so each line ends with a line feed, except a\nlast line without one; carriage returns of CRLF line endings are kept as part of the line. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=:), intent(out), allocatable :: text the input Calls proc~~read_stdin~~CallsGraph proc~read_stdin read_stdin proc~builder_append string_builder_t%builder_append proc~read_stdin->proc~builder_append proc~builder_get string_builder_t%builder_get proc~read_stdin->proc~builder_get Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~read_stdin~~CalledByGraph proc~read_stdin read_stdin proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~read_stdin proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine read_stdin ( text ) !! All of standard input. Lines are read as text, so each line ends with a line feed, except a !! last line without one; carriage returns of CRLF line endings are kept as part of the line. use , intrinsic :: iso_fortran_env , only : input_unit use ffmt_strings , only : string_builder_t character ( len = :), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: text !! the input type ( string_builder_t ) :: buf character ( len = 4096 ) :: chunk integer :: ios , n do read ( input_unit , '(a)' , advance = 'no' , iostat = ios , size = n ) chunk call buf % append ( chunk ( 1 : n )) if ( is_iostat_eor ( ios )) then call buf % append ( achar ( 10 )) else if ( ios /= 0 ) then exit ! end of input end if end do text = buf % get () end subroutine read_stdin","tags":"","url":"proc/read_stdin.html"},{"title":"write_file – fformat","text":"public  subroutine write_file(path, text, stat, errmsg) Replace the contents of file path (created if needed) with the bytes of text . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: path the file to write character(len=*), intent(in) :: text the new contents integer, intent(out) :: stat iostat of the open or write: nonzero on failure character(len=:), intent(out), allocatable :: errmsg the system's message, if stat is nonzero Called by proc~~write_file~~CalledByGraph proc~write_file write_file proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~write_file proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine write_file ( path , text , stat , errmsg ) !! Replace the contents of file `path` (created if needed) with the bytes of `text`. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path !! the file to write character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: text !! the new contents integer , intent ( out ) :: stat !! `iostat` of the open or write: nonzero on failure character ( len = :), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: errmsg !! the system's message, if `stat` is nonzero integer :: unit character ( len = 256 ) :: msg open ( newunit = unit , file = path , access = 'stream' , form = 'unformatted' , status = 'replace' , & action = 'write' , iostat = stat , iomsg = msg ) if ( stat /= 0 ) then errmsg = trim ( msg ) return end if write ( unit , iostat = stat , iomsg = msg ) text if ( stat /= 0 ) errmsg = trim ( msg ) close ( unit ) end subroutine write_file","tags":"","url":"proc/write_file.html"},{"title":"compute_case – fformat","text":"public  function compute_case(source, views, opts) result(marks) The letter case wanted for each token. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( source_t ), intent(in) :: source the source type( statement_view_t ), intent(in) :: views (:) the view of each item (see statement_views ) type( case_options_t ), intent(in) :: opts the case wanted for each category Return Value type( case_marks_t ) Calls proc~~compute_case~~CallsGraph proc~compute_case compute_case proc~kind_part kind_part proc~compute_case->proc~kind_part proc~names_case names_case proc~compute_case->proc~names_case proc~statement_case statement_case proc~compute_case->proc~statement_case proc~view_kind_of statement_view_t%view_kind_of proc~names_case->proc~view_kind_of proc~view_word statement_view_t%view_word proc~names_case->proc~view_word proc~view_closing statement_view_t%view_closing proc~statement_case->proc~view_closing proc~statement_case->proc~view_kind_of proc~statement_case->proc~view_word Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~compute_case~~CalledByGraph proc~compute_case compute_case proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~compute_case proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code function compute_case ( source , views , opts ) result ( marks ) !! The letter case wanted for each token. type ( source_t ), intent ( in ) :: source !! the source type ( statement_view_t ), intent ( in ) :: views (:) !! the view of each item (see [[statement_views]]) type ( case_options_t ), intent ( in ) :: opts !! the case wanted for each category type ( case_marks_t ) :: marks integer :: k , t , a , b allocate ( marks % whole ( source % tokens % n ), marks % part ( source % tokens % n )) marks % whole = CASE_KEEP marks % part = CASE_KEEP do t = 1 , source % tokens % n associate ( tok => source % tokens % tok ( t )) select case ( tok % kind ) case ( TK_DOTOP ) marks % whole ( t ) = opts % operators case ( TK_INT , TK_REAL ) marks % whole ( t ) = opts % types ! their only letters: an exponent and a kind end select if ( opts % types /= CASE_KEEP . and . ( tok % kind == TK_DOTOP . or . tok % kind == TK_STRING )) then call kind_part ( source % text ( tok % first : tok % last ), tok % kind , a , b ) if ( b >= a ) marks % part ( t ) = opts % types end if end associate end do do k = 1 , source % stmts % n if ( source % stmts % s ( k )% kind /= SK_CODE ) cycle if ( opts % keywords /= CASE_KEEP ) call statement_case ( views ( k ), opts % keywords , marks % whole ) if ( opts % procedures /= CASE_KEEP . or . opts % constants /= CASE_KEEP . or . opts % types /= CASE_KEEP ) & call names_case ( views ( k ), opts , marks % whole ) end do end function compute_case","tags":"","url":"proc/compute_case.html"},{"title":"kind_part – fformat","text":"public pure subroutine kind_part(text, kind, a, b) Where the kind is in the text of a token of kind kind : text(a:b) , or b < a if it has none.\nFor a logical constant it is the suffix ( _lk in .true._lk ), for a string the prefix ( ck in ck_'a' ). Numbers have letters only in their exponent and kind, so they are cased whole. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: text the token's text integer, intent(in) :: kind its kind ( TK_* ) integer, intent(out) :: a the range of the kind in text integer, intent(out) :: b the range of the kind in text Called by proc~~kind_part~~CalledByGraph proc~kind_part kind_part proc~compute_case compute_case proc~compute_case->proc~kind_part proc~emit_body emit_body proc~emit_body->proc~kind_part proc~emit_continuation emit_continuation proc~emit_continuation->proc~emit_body proc~emit_statement emit_statement proc~emit_statement->proc~emit_body proc~emit_statement->proc~emit_continuation proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~compute_case proc~layout layout proc~format_pass->proc~layout proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~layout->proc~emit_statement proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure subroutine kind_part ( text , kind , a , b ) !! Where the kind is in the text of a token of kind `kind`: `text(a:b)`, or `b < a` if it has none. !! For a logical constant it is the suffix (`_lk` in `.true._lk`), for a string the prefix (`ck` in !! `ck_'a'`). Numbers have letters only in their exponent and kind, so they are cased whole. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: text !! the token's text integer , intent ( in ) :: kind !! its kind (`TK_*`) integer , intent ( out ) :: a , b !! the range of the kind in `text` integer :: p a = 1 b = 0 select case ( kind ) case ( TK_DOTOP ) p = index ( text , '.' , back = . true .) if ( p > 1 . and . p < len ( text )) then if ( text ( p + 1 : p + 1 ) == '_' ) then a = p + 2 b = len ( text ) end if end if case ( TK_STRING ) p = scan ( text , '\"' // \"'\" ) if ( p > 2 ) then if ( text ( p - 1 : p - 1 ) == '_' ) b = p - 2 end if end select end subroutine kind_part","tags":"","url":"proc/kind_part.html"},{"title":"names_case – fformat","text":"private  subroutine names_case(v, opts, mode) Mark the intrinsic procedures, the constants of the intrinsic modules and the kinds named in\none code statement. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( statement_view_t ), intent(in) :: v the statement type( case_options_t ), intent(in) :: opts the case wanted for each category integer, intent(inout) :: mode (:) case mode of each token, set for the names Calls proc~~names_case~~CallsGraph proc~names_case names_case proc~view_kind_of statement_view_t%view_kind_of proc~names_case->proc~view_kind_of proc~view_word statement_view_t%view_word proc~names_case->proc~view_word Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~names_case~~CalledByGraph proc~names_case names_case proc~compute_case compute_case proc~compute_case->proc~names_case proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~compute_case proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine names_case ( v , opts , mode ) !! Mark the intrinsic procedures, the constants of the intrinsic modules and the kinds named in !! one code statement. type ( statement_view_t ), intent ( in ) :: v !! the statement type ( case_options_t ), intent ( in ) :: opts !! the case wanted for each category integer , intent ( inout ) :: mode (:) !! case mode of each token, set for the names integer :: j , first logical :: decl , use_stmt , entity if ( v % n == 0 ) return first = v % first if ( first + 1 < v % n ) then if ( v % kind_of ( first ) == TK_NAME . and . v % is ( first + 1 , ':' )) first = first + 2 ! construct name end if use_stmt = v % is ( first , 'use' ) decl = . false . if (. not . use_stmt ) decl = any ([( v % is ( j , '::' ) . and . v % depth ( j ) == 0 , j = 1 , v % n )]) entity = . false . ! after `::`, the next top-level name is an entity being declared do j = first , v % n if ( decl . and . v % depth ( j ) == 0 ) then if ( v % is ( j , '::' ) . or . ( entity . and . v % is ( j , ',' ))) then entity = . true . cycle end if end if if ( v % kinds ( j ) /= TK_NAME ) cycle if ( j == first ) cycle if ( v % is ( j - 1 , '%' )) cycle if ( decl . and . entity . and . v % depth ( j ) == 0 . and . ( v % is ( j - 1 , '::' ) . or . v % is ( j - 1 , ',' ))) cycle select case ( v % word ( j - 1 )) case ( 'function' , 'subroutine' , 'procedure' , 'entry' , 'program' , 'module' , 'submodule' , 'interface' ) cycle end select if ( opts % procedures /= CASE_KEEP . and . ( v % is ( j + 1 , '(' ) . or . v % is ( j - 1 , 'call' ))) then if ( any ( INTRINSIC_PROCEDURES == v % word ( j ))) mode ( v % code ( j )) = opts % procedures end if if ( opts % constants /= CASE_KEEP . and . . not . v % is ( j + 1 , '=' )) then if ( any ( INTRINSIC_CONSTANTS == v % word ( j ))) mode ( v % code ( j )) = opts % constants end if if ( opts % types /= CASE_KEEP . and . is_kind ( j )) mode ( v % code ( j )) = opts % types end do contains logical function is_kind ( j ) !! True if name `j` is a kind: the value of `kind=`, or the kind of the type that starts a !! declaration (`real(dp) :: x`, `integer(int64), parameter :: n = 1`). integer , intent ( in ) :: j !! index into `v%code(:)` is_kind = v % is ( j - 1 , '=' ) . and . v % is ( j - 2 , 'kind' ) if ( is_kind . or . . not . decl ) return if ( j - 2 /= first . or . . not . v % is ( j - 1 , '(' ) . or . . not . v % is ( j + 1 , ')' )) return select case ( v % word ( first )) case ( 'integer' , 'real' , 'complex' , 'logical' , 'character' ) is_kind = . true . end select end function is_kind end subroutine names_case","tags":"","url":"proc/names_case.html"},{"title":"statement_case – fformat","text":"private  subroutine statement_case(v, kw_mode, mode) Mark the keywords of one code statement with kw_mode . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( statement_view_t ), intent(in) :: v the statement integer, intent(in) :: kw_mode case mode for keywords integer, intent(inout) :: mode (:) case mode of each token, set for the keywords Calls proc~~statement_case~~CallsGraph proc~statement_case statement_case proc~view_closing statement_view_t%view_closing proc~statement_case->proc~view_closing proc~view_kind_of statement_view_t%view_kind_of proc~statement_case->proc~view_kind_of proc~view_word statement_view_t%view_word proc~statement_case->proc~view_word Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~statement_case~~CalledByGraph proc~statement_case statement_case proc~compute_case compute_case proc~compute_case->proc~statement_case proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~compute_case proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine statement_case ( v , kw_mode , mode ) !! Mark the keywords of one code statement with `kw_mode`. type ( statement_view_t ), intent ( in ) :: v !! the statement integer , intent ( in ) :: kw_mode !! case mode for keywords integer , intent ( inout ) :: mode (:) !! case mode of each token, set for the keywords integer :: k if ( v % n == 0 ) return k = v % first if ( k + 1 < v % n ) then if ( v % kind_of ( k ) == TK_NAME . and . v % is ( k + 1 , ':' )) k = k + 2 ! construct name end if if ( v % is ( k , 'format' )) return call leading ( k ) call attributes ( k ) call trailing ( k ) contains subroutine attributes ( k ) !! Mark the attributes of a declaration: the word after each top-level `,` before `::`, and !! `in`, `out` and `inout` in `intent(...)`. integer , intent ( in ) :: k !! index into `v%code(:)` of the first word of the statement integer :: j if (. not . any ([( v % is ( j , '::' ) . and . v % depth ( j ) == 0 , j = 1 , v % n )])) return do j = k , v % n if ( v % depth ( j ) > 0 ) cycle if ( v % is ( j , '::' )) exit if ( v % is ( j , ',' ) . and . is_keyword ( j + 1 )) then call mark ( j + 1 ) if ( v % is ( j + 1 , 'intent' )) call intent_args ( j + 2 ) end if end do end subroutine attributes subroutine trailing ( k ) !! Mark the keywords after the leading ones: `only` of a `use` statement, and `result` and !! `bind` after a parenthesis. integer , intent ( in ) :: k !! index into `v%code(:)` of the first word of the statement integer :: j do j = k + 1 , v % n if ( v % depth ( j ) > 0 ) cycle select case ( v % word ( j )) case ( 'only' ) if ( v % is ( j + 1 , ':' ) . and . v % is ( j - 1 , ',' )) call mark ( j ) case ( 'result' , 'bind' ) if ( v % is ( j - 1 , ')' ) . and . v % is ( j + 1 , '(' )) call mark ( j ) end select end do end subroutine trailing subroutine mark ( j ) !! Give code token `j` the keyword case mode, if it is inside the statement. integer , intent ( in ) :: j !! index into `v%code(:)` if ( j >= 1 . and . j <= v % n ) mode ( v % code ( j )) = kw_mode end subroutine mark logical function is_keyword ( j ) !! True if code token `j` is a name spelled like a keyword (including `endif`, `enddo`, ...). integer , intent ( in ) :: j !! index into `v%code(:)` character ( len = :), allocatable :: w is_keyword = . false . if ( v % kind_of ( j ) /= TK_NAME ) return w = v % word ( j ) if ( any ( KEYWORDS == w )) then is_keyword = . true . else if ( len ( w ) > 3 ) then if ( w ( 1 : 3 ) == 'end' ) is_keyword = any ( KEYWORDS == w ( 4 :)) . or . w ( 4 :) == 'blockdata' end if if ( w == 'blockdata' ) is_keyword = . true . end function is_keyword integer function after_parens ( j ) result ( next ) !! Index after the parenthesis group that opens at `j`, or `j` if there is none there. integer , intent ( in ) :: j !! index into `v%code(:)`