se if ( c == '&' . and . only_blanks_to_eol ( src , j + 1 )) then ! character context continued on the next line k = line_end ( src , j ) + 1 ! the line break if ( k > len ( src )) then j = len ( src ) flags = ior ( flags , STR_UNTERMINATED ) return end if if ( src ( k : k ) == CR . and . peek ( src , k + 1 ) == LF ) k = k + 1 k = k + 1 ! start of the continuation line flags = ior ( flags , STR_MULTILINE ) j = k do while ( is_blank ( peek ( src , j ))) j = j + 1 end do if ( peek ( src , j ) == '&' ) then j = j + 1 else flags = ior ( flags , STR_RAW_CONT ) j = k end if else j = j + 1 end if end do end function string_end","tags":"","url":"proc/string_end.html"},{"title":"add – fformat","text":"private  subroutine add(tokens, lx, src, kind, first, last, sub) Append a token, maintaining the line count and the glue state for split tokens. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( token_list_t ), intent(inout) :: tokens token list to append to type( lexer_t ), intent(inout) :: lx lexer state character(len=*), intent(in) :: src source text integer, intent(in) :: kind token kind, one of the TK_* constants integer, intent(in) :: first first byte of the token in src integer, intent(in) :: last last byte of the token in src integer, intent(in), optional :: sub sub-kind (CM_ , CT_ , STR_*); 0 if absent Calls proc~~add~~CallsGraph proc~add add proc~is_blank is_blank proc~add->proc~is_blank proc~is_code_char is_code_char proc~add->proc~is_code_char proc~peek peek proc~add->proc~peek proc~push token_list_t%push proc~add->proc~push proc~is_code_char->proc~is_blank Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that 