ace in a parent module. Source Code elemental logical function is_word ( kind ) !! Tokens that would run together with a following word: names, numbers and BOZ literals. integer , intent ( in ) :: kind !! token kind (`TK_*`) is_word = kind == TK_NAME . or . kind == TK_INT . or . kind == TK_REAL . or . kind == TK_BOZ end function is_word","tags":"","url":"proc/is_word.html"},{"title":"comment_gaps – fformat","text":"private  subroutine comment_gaps(source, spacing, gap) Ask for spacing blanks before each trailing comment (one after code or a continuation & ),\nunless a trailing comment on the line before or after starts in the same column: comments\nlined up in a column are left as they are. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( source_t ), intent(in) :: source the source integer, intent(in) :: spacing blanks wanted before a trailing comment integer, intent(inout) :: gap (:) gap wanted before each token, set for the comments Calls proc~~comment_gaps~~CallsGraph proc~comment_gaps comment_gaps proc~utf8_width utf8_width proc~comment_gaps->proc~utf8_width Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~comment_gaps~~CalledByGraph proc~comment_gaps comment_gaps proc~compute_gaps compute_gaps proc~compute_gaps->proc~comment_gaps proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~compute_gaps proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_