ementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code function split_long_lines ( src , line_length , indent , nsplit , changed ) result ( out ) !! `src` with each code line longer than `line_length` split once. The new continuation lines are indented !! by `indent` more than the line they come from if it is the first line of a statement, and like !! it if it is a continuation line, which the layout pass will usually leave in place. `nsplit` !! returns the number of splits. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: src !! the source text integer , intent ( in ) :: line_length !! maximum line width, in characters integer , intent ( in ) :: indent !! indentation step, in blanks integer , intent ( out ) :: nsplit !! number of lines split integer , allocatable , intent ( out ), optional :: changed (:, :) !! where the statements that were split !! are in `out`: bytes `changed(1, j):changed(2, j)`. !! Not allocated if one of them cannot be laid out !! again on its own (see [[stands_alone]]) character ( len = :), allocatable :: out type ( source_t ) :: source type ( string_builder_t ) :: buf character ( len = :), allocatable :: nl integer :: k , j , lend , a , p , q , base , start_col , offset , ncont , before , start , nranges integer , allocatable :: ranges (:, :) logical :: alone nsplit = 0 call parse_source ( src , source ) nl = achar ( 10 ) do j = 1 , source % tokens % n if ( source % tokens % tok ( j )% kind == TK_NEWLINE ) then nl = token_text ( src , source % tokens % tok ( j )) exit end if end do allocate ( ranges ( 2 , 16 )) nranges = 0 alone = . true . do k = 1 , source % stmts % n before = nsplit start = buf % length () + 1 if ( source % keep ( k ) . or . source % stmts % s ( k )% kind /= SK_CODE ) then call copy ( source % stmts % s ( k )% first , source % stmts % s ( k )% last ) cycle end if associate ( s => source % stmts % s ( k )) ncont = count ( source % tokens % tok ( s % first : s % last )% kind == TK_CONT . and . & source % tokens % tok ( s % first : s % last )% sub == CT_TRAILING ) end associate j = source % stmts % s ( k )% first do while ( j <= source % stmts % s ( k )% last ) lend = j do while ( lend < source % stmts % s ( k )% last ) if ( source % tokens % tok ( lend )% kind == TK_NEWLINE ) exit lend = lend + 1 end do ! split the line once; the rest is aligned by the next layout pass and split again if needed a = j start_col = column ( j ) base = indentation ( j ) offset = merge ( indent , 0 , j == source % stmts % s ( k )% first ) p = 0 if ( ncont < MAX_CONTINUATIONS ) p = break_point ( source % tokens , src , a , lend , start_col , line_length ) if ( p > 0 ) then ncont = ncont + 1 call copy ( a , p ) call buf % append ( ' &' // nl // repeat ( ' ' , base + offset )) nsplit = nsplit + 1 q = p + 1 do while ( source % tokens % tok ( q )% kind == TK_SPACE ) q = q + 1 end do a = q end if call copy ( a , lend ) j = lend + 1 end do if ( nsplit > before ) then if ( nranges == size ( ranges , 2 )) ranges = reshape ([ ranges , ranges ], [ 2 , 2 * nranges ]) nranges = nranges + 1 ranges (:, nranges ) = [ start , buf % length ()] alone = alone . and . stands_alone ( source , k ) end if end do out = buf % get () if ( present ( changed ) . and . alone ) changed = ranges (:, 1 : nranges ) contains subroutine copy ( first , last ) !! Append the text of tokens `first:last` to the output. integer , intent ( in ) :: first , last !! token range integer :: t do t = first , last call buf % append ( token_text ( src , source % tokens % tok ( t ))) end do end subroutine copy integer function column ( t ) !! Column of token `t` in `src`. integer , intent ( in ) :: t !! index into the token list integer :: i i = scan ( src ( 1 : source % tokens % tok ( t )% first - 1 ), achar ( 10 ) // achar ( 13 ), back = . true .) column = utf8_width ( src ( i + 1 : source % tokens % tok ( t )% first - 1 )) end function column integer function indentation ( t ) !! Indentation of the line containing token `t`. integer , intent ( in ) :: t !! index into the token list integer :: i , m i = scan ( src ( 1 : source % tokens % tok ( t )% first - 1 ), achar ( 10 ) // achar ( 13 ), back = . true .) + 1 m = verify ( src ( i :), ' ' // achar ( 9 )) if ( m == 0 ) then indentation = 0 else indentation = m - 1 end if end function indentation end function split_long_lines","tags":"","url":"proc/split_long_lines.html"},{"title":"stands_alone – fformat","text":"private pure function stands_alone(source, k) True if statement k of source , a code statement, can be laid out again on its own after\none of its lines is split, giving what laying out the whole text would: it takes up whole\nlines (no ; before or after it on its lines, no byte order mark), has no statement label\n(which stays at the start of the line), and is not followed by a comment line that may be\nlined up with a comment at the end of its last line. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( source_t ), intent(in) :: source the source integer, intent(in) :: k index into source%stmts Return Value logical Called by proc~~stands_alone~~CalledByGraph proc~stands_alone stands_alone proc~split_long_lines split_long_lines proc~split_long_lines->proc~stands_alone proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~split_long_lines proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure logical function stands_alone ( source , k ) !! True if statement `k` of `source`, a code statement, can be laid out again on its own after !! one of its lines is split, giving what laying out the whole text would: it takes up whole !! lines (no `;` before or after it on its lines, no byte order mark), has no statement label !! (which stays at the start of the line), and is not followed by a comment line that may be !! lined up with a comment at the end of its last line. type ( source_t ), intent ( in ) :: source !! the source integer , intent ( in ) :: k !! index into `source%stmts` integer :: j , f stands_alone = . false . associate ( s => source % stmts % s ( k ), tok => source % tokens % tok ) if ( s % first > 1 ) then if ( tok ( s % first - 1 )% kind /= TK_NEWLINE ) return end if if ( tok ( s % last )% kind /= TK_NEWLINE . and . s % last < source % tokens % n ) return if ( any ( tok ( s % first : s % last )% kind == TK_BOM )) return f = s % first do while ( f < s % last . and . tok ( f )% kind == TK_SPACE ) f = f + 1 end do if ( tok ( f )% kind == TK_INT ) return ! a statement label if ( k < source % stmts % n ) then if ( source % stmts % s ( k + 1 )% kind == SK_COMMENT ) then ! a comment at the end of the last line, before its line break j = s % last if ( tok ( j )% kind == TK_NEWLINE ) j = j - 1 if ( j >= s % first . and . tok ( j )% kind == TK_COMMENT ) return end if end if end associate stands_alone = . true . end function stands_alone","tags":"","url":"proc/stands_alone.html"},{"title":"closes – fformat","text":"private pure function closes(closing, open) True if an end of kind closing ends the open construct open . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: closing construct named by the end ( C_ANY for a bare end ) integer, intent(in) :: open construct that is open Return Value logical Called by pr