rcase text): PP_IF , PP_ELSE ( #elif , #else ), PP_ENDIF or PP_OTHER . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: text text of the preprocessor token, in lowercase Return Value integer Called by proc~~conditional_kind~~CalledByGraph proc~conditional_kind conditional_kind proc~analyze_structure analyze_structure proc~analyze_structure->proc~conditional_kind proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~analyze_structure proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure integer function conditional_kind ( text ) result ( kind ) !! Kind of a preprocessor line (lowercase text): `PP_IF`, `PP_ELSE` (`#elif`, `#else`), `PP_ENDIF` !! or `PP_OTHER`. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: text !! text of the preprocessor token, in lowercase character ( len = :), allocatable :: directive integer :: i , j kind = PP_OTHER i = 2 ! after '#' if ( len ( text ) < 2 . or . text ( 1 : 1 ) /= '#' ) return if ( text ( 2 : 2 ) == ':' ) i = 3 ! fypp do while ( i <= len ( text )) if ( text ( i : i ) /= ' ' . and . text ( i : i ) /= achar ( 9 )) exit i = i + 1 end do j = i do while ( j <= len ( text )) if ( text ( j : j ) < 'a' . or . text ( j : j ) > 'z' ) exit j = j + 1 end do directive = text ( i : j - 1 ) select case ( directive ) case ( 'if' , 'ifdef' , 'ifndef' ) kind = PP_IF case ( 'elif' , 'else' ) kind = PP_ELSE case ( 'endif' ) kind = PP_ENDIF end select end function conditional_kind","tags":"","url":"proc/conditional_kind.html"},{"title":"fypp_depths – fformat","text":"private  function fypp_depths(source) result(fypp) The number of fypp blocks around each item of source . The directives are counted wherever\nthey are, also inside a continued statement; a directive line itself is at the level outside\nits block, like else and end statements. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( source_t ), intent(in) :: source the source Return Value integer, allocatable, (:) Calls proc~~fypp_depths~~CallsGraph proc~fypp_depths fypp_depths proc~fypp_kind fypp_kind proc~fypp_depths->proc~fypp_kind proc~token_lower token_lower proc~fypp_depths->proc~token_lower proc~make_lowercase make_lowercase proc~token_lower->proc~make_lowercase Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~fypp_depths~~CalledByGraph proc~fypp_depths fypp_depths proc~analyze_structure analyze_structure proc~analyze_structure->proc~fypp_depths proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~analyze_structure proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code function fypp_depths ( source ) result ( fypp ) !! The number of fypp blocks around each item of `source`. The directives are counted wherever !! they are, also inside a continued statement; a directive line itself is at the level outside !! its block, like `else` and `end` statements. type ( source_t ), intent ( in ) :: source !! the source integer , allocatable :: fypp (:) integer :: k , j , d allocate ( fypp ( source % stmts % n )) d = 0 do k = 1 , source % stmts % n fypp ( k ) = d do j = source % stmts % s ( k )% first , source % stmts % s ( k )% last if ( source % tokens % tok ( j )% kind /= TK_PREPROC ) cycle select case ( fypp_kind ( token_lower ( source % text , source % tokens % tok ( j )))) case ( FY_OPEN ) d = d + 1 case ( FY_MIDDLE ) if ( source % stmts % s ( k )% kind == SK_PREPROC ) fypp ( k ) = max ( 0 , d - 1 ) case ( FY_CLOSE ) d = max ( 0 , d - 1 ) if ( source % stmts % s ( k )% kind == SK_PREPROC ) fypp ( k ) = d end select end do end do end function fypp_depths","tags":"","url":"proc/fypp_depths.html"},{"title":"fypp_kind – fformat","text":"private pure function fypp_kind(text) result(kind) Kind of a preprocessor line (lowercase text) as a fypp block directive: one of the FY_*\nconstants. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: text text of the preprocessor token, in lowercase Return Value integer Called by proc~~fypp_kind~~CalledByGraph proc~fypp_kind fypp_kind proc~fypp_depths fypp_depths proc~fypp_depths->proc~fypp_kind proc~analyze_structure analyze_structure proc~analyze_structure->proc~fypp_depths proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~analyze_structure proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure integer function fypp_kind ( text ) result ( kind ) !! Kind of a preprocessor line (lowercase text) as a fypp block directive: one of the FY_* !! constants. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: text !! text of the preprocessor token, in lowercase integer :: i , j kind = FY_OTHER if ( len ( text ) < 3 ) return if ( text ( 1 : 2 ) /= '#:' ) return i = 3 do while ( i <= len ( text )) if ( text ( i : i ) /= ' ' . and . text ( i : i ) /= achar ( 9 )) exit i = i + 1 end do j = i do while ( j <= len ( text )) if ( text ( j : j ) < 'a' . or . text ( j : j ) > 'z' ) exit j = j + 1 end do select case ( text ( i : j - 1 )) case ( 'if' , 'for' , 'def' , 'block' , 'call' , 'mute' ) kind = FY_OPEN case ( 'elif' , 'else' , 'nextarg' ) kind = FY_MIDDLE case ( 'endif' , 'endfor' , 'enddef' , 'endblock' , 'endcall' , 'endmute' ) kind = FY_CLOSE end select end function fypp_kind","tags":"","url":"proc/fypp_kind.html"},{"title":"middle_fits – fformat","text":"private pure function middle_fits(middle, open) True if a middle statement of construct middle ( else of C_IF , contains , ...) may\nappear directly inside the open construct open . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: middle construct of the middle statement integer, intent(in) :: open construct that is open Return Value logical Called by proc~~middle_fits~~CalledByGraph proc~middle_fits middle_fits proc~analyze_structure analyze_structure proc~analyze_structure->proc~middle_fits proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~analyze_structure proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure logical function middle_fits ( middle , open ) !! True if a middle statement of construct `middle` (`else` of `C_IF`, `contains`, ...) may !! appear directly inside the open construct `open`. integer , intent ( in ) :: middle !! construct of the middle statement integer , intent ( in ) :: open !! construct that is open select case ( middle ) case ( C_CONTAINS ) select case ( open ) case ( C_PROGRAM , C_MODULE , C_SUBMODULE , C_SUBROUTINE , C_FUNCTION , C_PROCEDURE , C_TYPE ) middle_fits = . true . case default middle_fits = . false . end select case default middle_fits = middle == open end select end function middle_fits","tags":"","url":"proc/middle_fits.html"},{"title":"stack_snapshot – fformat","text":"private pure function stack_snapshot(self) result(scopes) The open constructs, outermost first. Type Bound scope_stack_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( scope_stack_t ), intent(in) :: self the stack Return Value type( scope_t ), allocatable, (:) Called by proc~~stack_snapshot~~CalledByGraph proc~stack_snapshot scope_stack_t%stack_snapshot proc~analyze_structure analyze_structure proc~analyze_structure->proc~stack_snapshot proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~analyze_structure proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure function stack_snapshot ( self ) result ( scopes ) !! The open constructs, outermost first. class ( scope_stack_t ), intent ( in ) :: self !! the stack type ( scope_t ), allocatable :: scopes (:) if ( allocated ( self % s )) then scopes = self % s ( 1 : self % top ) else allocate ( scopes ( 0 )) end if end function stack_snapshot","tags":"","url":"proc/stack_snapshot.html"},{"title":"analyze_structure – fformat","text":"public  subroutine analyze_structure(source, views, st, diags) Classify every statement and compute its depth: the number of constructs enclosing it, and\nhow many of those are program units and procedures, so callers can choose not to indent\ntheir bodies.\nAn opening statement is at the depth outside its construct, the statements inside are one\ndeeper, and middle ( else , contains , ...) and closing statements are at the opening depth.\nNon-code items get the depth of the code around them. Branches of preprocessor conditionals (cpp #if / #ifdef / #elif / #else / #endif and\nfypp #:if / #:elif / #:else / #:endif ) are treated as alternatives: each branch starts\nfrom the structure at the #if , and the structure at the end of the first branch carries\non after the #endif . That keeps code such as #ifdef X / do / #endif ... #ifdef X / end do / #endif balanced. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( source_t ), intent(in) :: source the source type( statement_view_t ), intent(in) :: views (:) the view of each item (see statement_views ) type( structure_t ), intent(out) :: st the structure type( diagnostic_t ), intent(out), allocatable :: diags (:)