int from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~analyze_structure~~CalledByGraph proc~analyze_structure analyze_structure proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~analyze_structure proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine analyze_structure ( source , views , st , diags ) !! Classify every statement and compute its depth: the number of constructs enclosing it, and !! how many of those are program units and procedures, so callers can choose not to indent !! their bodies. !! An opening statement is at the depth outside its construct, the statements inside are one !! deeper, and middle (`else`, `contains`, ...) and closing statements are at the opening depth. !! Non-code items get the depth of the code around them. !! !! Branches of preprocessor conditionals (cpp `#if`/`#ifdef`/`#elif`/`#else`/`#endif` and !! fypp `#:if`/`#:elif`/`#:else`/`#:endif`) are treated as alternatives: each branch starts !! from the structure at the `#if`, and the structure at the end of the first branch carries !! on after the `#endif`. That keeps code such as `#ifdef X` / `do` / `#endif` ... `#ifdef X` / !! `end do` / `#endif` balanced. type ( source_t ), intent ( in ) :: source !! the source type ( statement_view_t ), intent ( in ) :: views (:) !! the view of each item (see [[statement_views]]) type ( structure_t ), intent ( out ) :: st !! the structure type ( diagnostic_t ), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: diags (:) !! structure problems found, in the order found type ( scope_stack_t ) :: stack type ( saved_stack_t ), allocatable :: saved (:) type ( stmt_info_t ), allocatable :: info (:) integer , allocatable :: depth (:), nunits (:), nprocs (:) integer :: k , line , nsaved logical :: in_interface associate ( n => source % stmts % n ) allocate ( info ( n ), depth ( n ), nunits ( n ), nprocs ( n ), diags ( 0 ), saved ( 0 )) end associate nsaved = 0 do k = 1 , source % stmts % n depth ( k ) = stack % top if ( source % stmts % s ( k )% kind == SK_PREPROC ) call preprocessor ( k ) if ( source % stmts % s ( k )% kind /= SK_CODE ) then call count_units ( k ) cycle end if line = source % tokens % tok ( source % stmts % s ( k )% first )% line in_interface = . false . if ( stack % top > 0 ) in_interface = stack % s ( stack % top )% construct == C_INTERFACE info ( k ) = classify_statement ( source % text , source % tokens , views ( k ), in_interface ) select case ( info ( k )% role ) case ( ROLE_OPEN ) call stack % push ( scope_t ( info ( k )% construct , info ( k )% do_label , line )) case ( ROLE_MIDDLE ) if ( stack % top == 0 . and . info ( k )% construct == C_CONTAINS ) then ! a main program without a `program` statement call stack % push ( scope_t ( C_PROGRAM , 0 , line )) else if ( stack % top == 0 ) then call diagnose ( line , construct_label ( info ( k )% construct ) // ' statement outside any construct' ) else if (. not . middle_fits ( info ( k )% construct , stack % s ( stack % top )% construct )) then call diagnose ( line , construct_label ( info ( k )% construct ) // ' statement inside ' // & opened ( stack % s ( stack % top ))) else depth ( k ) = stack % top - 1 end if case ( ROLE_CLOSE ) call close_scope ( info ( k )% construct , line ) depth ( k ) = stack % top end select call count_units ( k ) ! the labeled statement that ends `do 10 ...` loops is part of the innermost loop body if ( info ( k )% label > 0 ) then do while ( stack % top > 0 ) if ( stack % s ( stack % top )% construct /= C_DO . or . stack % s ( stack % top )% do_label /= info ( k )% label ) exit stack % top = stack % top - 1 end do end if end do do k = stack % top , 1 , - 1 call diagnose ( stack % s ( k )% line , construct_label ( stack % s ( k )% construct ) // ' is not closed' ) end do call move_alloc ( info , st % info ) call move_alloc ( depth , st % depth ) call move_alloc ( nunits , st % units ) call move_alloc ( nprocs , st % procedures ) st % fypp = fypp_depths ( source ) contains subroutine count_units ( k ) !! Record how many of the scopes enclosing item `k` are program units, and procedures. integer , intent ( in ) :: k !! index into `stmts` integer :: j nunits ( k ) = 0 nprocs ( k ) = 0 do j = 1 , depth ( k ) select case ( stack % s ( j )% construct ) case ( C_MODULE , C_SUBMODULE , C_PROGRAM ) nunits ( k ) = nunits ( k ) + 1 case ( C_SUBROUTINE , C_FUNCTION , C_PROCEDURE ) ! interface bodies are declarations, not procedure definitions if ( j == 1 ) then nprocs ( k ) = nprocs ( k ) + 1 else if ( stack % s ( j - 1 )% construct /= C_INTERFACE ) then nprocs ( k ) = nprocs ( k ) + 1 end if end select end do end subroutine count_units subroutine preprocessor ( k ) !! Save or restore the scope stack at the preprocessor conditionals in item `k`, and set !! the depth of the item to that of the restored stack. integer , intent ( in ) :: k !! index into `stmts` of a preprocessor item integer :: j do j = source % stmts % s ( k )% first , source % stmts % s ( k )% last if ( source % tokens % tok ( j )% kind /= TK_PREPROC ) cycle select case ( conditional_kind ( token_lower ( source % text , source % tokens % tok ( j )))) case ( PP_IF ) nsaved = nsaved + 1 if ( nsaved > size ( saved )) saved = [ saved , saved_stack_t ()] saved ( nsaved )% at_if = stack % snapshot () if ( allocated ( saved ( nsaved )% after_first )) deallocate ( saved ( nsaved )% after_first ) case ( PP_ELSE ) if ( nsaved > 0 ) then if (. not . allocated ( saved ( nsaved )% after_first )) saved ( nsaved )% after_first = stack % snapshot () call stack % restore ( saved ( nsaved )% at_if ) depth ( k ) = stack % top end if case ( PP_ENDIF ) if ( nsaved > 0 ) then if ( allocated ( saved ( nsaved )% after_first )) call stack % restore ( saved ( nsaved )% after_first ) depth ( k ) = stack % top nsaved = nsaved - 1 end if end select end do end subroutine preprocessor subroutine close_scope ( construct , line ) !! Pop the construct closed by an `end` statement, with a diagnostic if it does not match !! the innermost open construct. If an outer one matches, everything down to it is closed. integer , intent ( in ) :: construct !! construct named by the `end` (`C_ANY` for a bare `end`) integer , intent ( in ) :: line !! source line of the `end` statement integer :: j if ( stack % top == 0 ) then ! `end` or `end program` may close a main program without a `program` statement if ( construct /= C_ANY . and . construct /= C_PROGRAM ) & call diagnose ( line , 'end ' // construct_label ( construct ) // ' without an open construct' ) return end if if ( closes ( construct , stack % s ( stack % top )% construct )) then stack % top = stack % top - 1 return end if ! recover from a missing `end`: close down to a matching construct if there is one do j = stack % top - 1 , 1 , - 1 if ( closes ( construct , stack % s ( j )% construct )) then call diagnose ( line , 'end ' // construct_label ( construct ) // ' closes ' // & opened 