signature]] would: same kind (operators all alike), same glue, and the same text, !! ignoring case where Fortran does (see [[folded_length]]), with relational operators in their !! symbol spelling. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: sa !! source text of `s` character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: sb !! source text of `t` type ( token_t ), intent ( in ) :: s !! a code token of `sa` type ( token_t ), intent ( in ) :: t !! a code token of `sb` integer :: ks , kt , k , nfold character ( len = :), allocatable :: ca , cb ks = s % kind kt = t % kind if ( ks == TK_DOTOP ) ks = TK_OP if ( kt == TK_DOTOP ) kt = TK_OP same_token = . false . if ( ks /= kt . or . ( s % glued . neqv . t % glued )) return if ( s % last - s % first == t % last - t % first ) then nfold = folded_length ( sa ( s % first : s % last ), s % kind ) same_token = . true . do k = 0 , s % last - s % first if ( k < nfold ) then if ( lower_char ( sa ( s % first + k : s % first + k )) == lower_char ( sb ( t % first + k : t % first + k ))) cycle else if ( sa ( s % first + k : s % first + k ) == sb ( t % first + k : t % first + k )) cycle end if same_token = . false . exit end do if ( same_token ) return end if ! `.lt.` and `<`: rare, so the allocating comparison is fine here if ( ks == TK_OP ) then ca = canonical_relational ( token_lower ( sa , s )) cb = canonical_relational ( token_lower ( sb , t )) same_token = len ( ca ) == len ( cb ) . and . ca == cb end if end function same_token","tags":"","url":"proc/same_token.html"},{"title":"too_long – fformat","text":"private pure function too_long(text, limit) True if a code line of text may be longer than limit characters (see longest_code ).\nA line has no more characters than bytes, so the scan is only needed when a line has more\nbytes than that, which finding the line breaks shows quickly. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: text the formatted text integer, intent(in) :: limit the line length Return Value logical Call