cedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine find_config ( dir , cfg , stat , errmsg ) !! The configuration for files in directory `dir` (an absolute path): from the nearest config file !! in `dir` or its parents. `cfg%path` is `''` if there is none. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: dir !! absolute path of the directory type ( config_t ), intent ( out ) :: cfg !! the configuration found integer , intent ( out ) :: stat !! nonzero if the config file found cannot be read character ( len = :), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: errmsg !! what is wrong, with the file name, if `stat` is nonzero character ( len = :), allocatable :: d , candidate logical :: exists , found stat = 0 d = dir do while ( len ( d ) > 0 ) candidate = join_path ( d , CONFIG_NAME ) inquire ( file = candidate , exist = exists ) if ( exists ) then call load_config ( candidate , . false ., cfg , found , stat , errmsg ) return end if candidate = join_path ( d , 'fpm.toml' ) inquire ( file = candidate , exist = exists ) if ( exists ) then call load_config ( candidate , . true ., cfg , found , stat , errmsg ) if ( found . or . stat /= 0 ) return end if if ( parent_directory ( d ) == d ) exit d = parent_directory ( d ) end do call empty ( cfg ) end subroutine find_config","tags":"","url":"proc/find_config.html"},{"title":"load_config – fformat","text":"public  subroutine load_config(path, fpm, cfg, found, stat, errmsg) Read the configuration in file path : the whole file, or with fpm its [extra.fformat] table. found is false if an fpm.toml has no such table. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: path the TOML file logical, intent(in) :: fpm path is an fpm.toml type( config_t ), intent(out) :: cfg the configuration; empty if not found logical, intent(out) :: found the file has a configuration integer, intent(out) :: stat nonzero for bad TOML, an unknown key or a bad value character(len=:), intent(out), allocatable :: errmsg what is wrong, with the file name, if stat is nonzero Calls proc~~load_config~~CallsGraph proc~load_config load_config get get proc~load_config->get get_keys get_keys proc~load_config->get_keys get_type get_type proc~load_config->get_type get_value get_value proc~load_config->get_value proc~empty empty proc~load_config->proc~empty proc~to_s to_s proc~load_config->proc~to_s toml_load toml_load proc~load_config->toml_load Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~load_config~~CalledByGraph proc~load_config load_config proc~config_for config_for proc~config_for->proc~load_config proc~find_config find_config proc~config_for->proc~find_config proc~find_config->proc~load_config proc~directory_files directory_files proc~directory_files->proc~config_for proc~options_for options_for proc~options_for->proc~config_for proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~options_for proc~run run proc~run->proc~directory_files proc~process_file process_file proc~run->proc~process_file proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~run->proc~process_stdin proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine load_config ( path , fpm , cfg , found , stat , errmsg ) !! Read the configuration in file `path`: the whole file, or with `fpm` its !! `[extra.fformat]` table. `found` is false if an `fpm.toml` has no such table. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path !! the TOML file logical , intent ( in ) :: fpm !! `path` is an `fpm.toml` type ( config_t ), intent ( out ) :: cfg !! the configuration; empty if not `found` logical , intent ( out ) :: found !! the file has a configuration integer , intent ( out ) :: stat !! nonzero for bad TOML, an unknown key or a bad value character ( len = :), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: errmsg !! what is wrong, with the file name, if `stat` is nonzero type ( toml_table ), allocatable , target :: top type ( toml_table ), pointer :: extra , table type ( toml_error ), allocatable :: error stat = 0 found = . false . call empty ( cfg ) call toml_load ( top , path , error = error ) if ( allocated ( error )) then stat = 1 errmsg = path // ': ' // error % message return end if if ( fpm ) then call get_value ( top , 'extra' , extra , requested = . false .) if (. not . associated ( extra )) return call get_value ( extra , 'fformat' , table , requested = . false .) if (. not . associated ( table )) return else table => top end if found = . true . cfg % path = path call read_table ( table , '' ) contains recursive subroutine read_table ( t , prefix ) !! Add the settings in table `t`, with keys prefixed by `prefix`. type ( toml_table ), intent ( inout ) :: t !! the table to read character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: prefix !! `''` for the top level, or `spaces.` / `case.` type ( toml_key ), allocatable :: keys (:) class ( toml_value ), pointer :: v type ( toml_table ), pointer :: sub character ( len = :), allocatable :: key , text integer :: k call t % get_keys ( keys ) do k = 1 , size ( keys ) key = keys ( k )% key call t % get ( key , v ) select type ( v ) type is ( toml_table ) sub => v if ( prefix == '' . and . key == 'files' ) then call read_files ( sub ) else if ( prefix == '' . and . ( key == 'spaces' . or . key == 'case' )) then call read_table ( sub , key // '.' ) else call bad ( 'unknown table \"' // prefix // key // '\"' ) end if type is ( toml_keyval ) text = value_text ( t , key , v % get_type ()) if ( stat /= 0 ) return ! `all` comes first, so that the other entries of the table override it if ( key == 'all' ) then cfg % settings = [ setting_t ( prefix // key , text ), cfg % settings ] else cfg % settings = [ cfg % settings , setting_t ( prefix // key , text )] end if class default call bad ( 'unexpected value for \"' // prefix // key // '\"' ) end select if ( stat /= 0 ) return end do end subroutine read_table function value_text ( t , key , kind ) result ( text ) !! A string, integer or boolean value as text. type ( toml_table ), intent ( inout ) :: t !! the table holding the value character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: key !! the value's key in `t` integer , intent ( in ) :: kind !! the value's type, a `toml_type` member character ( len = :), allocatable :: text integer :: i logical :: flag text = '' if ( kind == toml_type % string ) then call get_value ( t , key , text ) else if ( kind == toml_type % int ) then call get_value ( t , key , i ) text = to_s ( i ) else if ( kind == toml_type % boolean ) then call get_value ( t , key , flag ) text = merge ( 'true ' , 'false' , flag ) text = trim ( text ) else call bad ( 'expected a string, number or true/false for \"' // key // '\"' ) end if end function value_text subroutine read_files ( t ) !! Read the `[files]` table `t` into `cfg%extensions` and `cfg%exclude`. type ( toml_table ), intent ( inout ) :: t !! the `[files]` table type ( toml_key ), allocatable :: keys (:) integer :: k call t % get_keys ( keys ) do k = 1 , size ( keys ) select case ( keys ( k )% key ) case ( 'extensions' ) call read_list ( t , 'extensions' , cfg % extensions ) case ( 'exclude' ) call read_list ( t , 'exclude' , cfg % exclude ) case default call bad ( 'unknown setting \"files.' // keys ( k )% key // '\"' ) end select if ( stat /= 0 ) return end do end subroutine read_files subroutine read_list ( t , key , list ) !! An array of strings. type ( toml_table ), intent ( inout ) :: t !! the `[files]` table character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: key !! the array's key in `t` type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: list (:) !! the strings, replacing any earlier list type ( toml_array ), pointer :: arr character ( len = :), allocatable :: item integer :: i , ios call get_value ( t , key , arr , requested = . false .) if (. not . associated ( arr )) then call bad ( 'expected a list of strings for \"files.' // key // '\"' ) return end if if ( allocated ( list )) deallocate ( list ) allocate ( list ( 0 )) do i = 1 , len ( arr ) call get_value ( arr , i , item , stat = ios ) if ( ios /= 0 . or . . not . allocated ( item )) then call bad ( 'expected a list of strings for \"files.' // key // '\"' ) return end if list = [ list , string_t ( item )] end do end subroutine read_list subroutine bad ( msg ) !! Make loading fail with message `msg`, prefixed with the file name. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: msg !! what is wrong stat = 1 errmsg = path // ': ' // msg end subroutine bad end subroutine load_config","tags":"","url":"proc/load_config.html"},{"title":"comment_column – fformat","text":"private  function comment_column(w, src, tokens, j, default) result