 the line break and !! without a trailing comment (compilers only limit the length of the code). A comment on a line !! of its own counts. type ( writer_t ), intent ( in ) :: w !! the output and the alignment state character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: src !! the source text type ( token_list_t ), intent ( in ) :: tokens !! its tokens integer , intent ( in ) :: first !! first token of the part of the line to measure integer , intent ( in ) :: lend !! last token of the line, its line break if it has one type ( piece_t ), allocatable :: pieces (:) integer :: k , j , before_blank call line_pieces ( w , src , tokens , first , lend , pieces ) width = 0 before_blank = 0 do k = 1 , size ( pieces ) if ( pieces ( k )% tok > 0 . and . k > 1 ) then if ( tokens % tok ( pieces ( k )% tok )% kind == TK_COMMENT ) then width = before_blank ! a trailing comment, and the blanks before it return end if end if if ( pieces ( k )% blanks > 0 ) then width = width + pieces ( k )% blanks cycle end if associate ( text => src ( pieces ( k )% first : pieces ( k )% last )) if ( pieces ( k )% tok > 0 ) before_blank = width + utf8_width ( text ) j = scan ( text , achar ( 10 ) // achar ( 13 )) if ( j > 0 ) then ! a line break, or a token continued on the next line width = width + utf8_width ( text ( 1 : j - 1 )) return end if width = width + utf8_width ( text ) end associate end do end function line_width","tags":"","url":"proc/line_width.html"},{"title":"to_case – fformat","text":"private pure function to_case(text, upper) result(t) text in ASCII upper or lower case. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: text the text to convert logical, intent(in) :: upper true for upper case, false for lower case Return Value character(len=len) Called by proc~~to_case~~CalledByGraph proc~to_case to_case proc~emit_body emit_body proc~emit_body->proc~to_case proc~emit_continuation emit_continuation proc~emit_continuation->proc~emit_body proc~emit_statement emit_statement 