h it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine emit_blank ( w , src , tokens , s ) !! A blank line: only its line break (and a byte order mark) is kept. type ( writer_t ), intent ( inout ) :: w !! the output and the alignment state character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: src !! the source text type ( token_list_t ), intent ( in ) :: tokens !! its tokens type ( statement_t ), intent ( in ) :: s !! the blank line item integer :: j do j = s % first , s % last if ( tokens % tok ( j )% kind == TK_NEWLINE . or . tokens % tok ( j )% kind == TK_BOM ) & call put ( w , token_text ( src , tokens % tok ( j ))) end do end subroutine emit_blank","tags":"","url":"proc/emit_blank.html"},{"title":"emit_body – fformat","text":"private  subroutine emit_body(w, src, tokens, first, lend) Tokens first:lend of a line (see line_pieces ), while tracking open brackets and the\nanchors for aligning continuation lines. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( writer_t ), intent(inout) :: w the output and the alignment state character(len=*), intent(in) :: src the source text type( token_list_t ), intent(in) :: tokens its tokens integer, intent(in) :: first first token to write integer, intent(in) :: lend last token of the line, its line break if it has one Calls proc~~emit_body~~CallsGraph proc~emit_body emit_body proc~input_column input_column proc~emit_body->proc~input_column proc~kind_part kind_part proc~emit_body->proc~kind_part proc~line_pieces line_pieces proc~emit_body->proc~line_pieces proc~put put proc~emit_body->proc~put proc~to_case to_case proc~emit_body->proc~to_case proc~token_lower token_lower proc~emit_body->proc~token_lower proc~utf8_width utf8_width proc~input_column->proc~utf8_width proc~builder_append string_builder_t%builder_append proc~put->proc~builder_append proc~put->proc~utf8_width proc~make_lowercase make_lowercase proc~token_lower->proc~make_lowercase Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~emit_body~~CalledByGraph proc~emit_body emit_body proc~emit_continuation emit_continuation proc~emit_continuation->proc~emit_body proc~emit_statement emit_statement proc~emit_statement->proc~emit_body proc~emit_statement->proc~emit_continuation proc~layout layout proc~layout->proc~emit_statement proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~layout proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine emit_body ( w , src , tokens , first , lend ) !! Tokens `first:lend` of a line (see [[line_pieces]]), while tracking open brackets and the !! anchors for aligning continuation lines. type ( writer_t ), intent ( inout ) :: w !! the output and the alignment state character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: src !! the source text type ( token_list_t ), intent ( in ) :: tokens !! its tokens integer , intent ( in ) :: first !! first token to write integer , intent ( in ) :: lend !! last token of the line, its line break if it has one type ( piece_t ), allocatable :: pieces (:) integer :: k , t , ka , kb character ( len = :), allocatable :: text call line_pieces ( w , src , tokens , first , lend , pieces ) do k = 1 , size ( pieces ) t = pieces ( k )% tok if ( pieces ( k )% blanks > 0 ) then call put ( w , repeat ( ' ' , pieces ( k )% blanks )) cycle end if if ( t == 0 ) then call put ( w , src ( pieces ( k )% first : pieces ( k )% last )) cycle end if if ( w % cases % whole ( t ) == CASE_KEEP . and . w % cases % part ( t ) == CASE_KEEP ) then call write_token ( t , src ( pieces ( k )% first : pieces ( k )% last )) ! without a copy cycle end if text = src ( pieces ( k )% first : pieces ( k )% last ) if ( w % cases % whole ( t ) /= CASE_KEEP ) text = to_case ( text , w % cases % whole ( t ) == CASE_UPPER ) if ( w % cases % part ( t ) /= CASE_KEEP ) then call kind_part ( text , tokens % tok ( t )% kind , ka , kb ) if ( kb >= ka ) text ( ka : kb ) = to_case ( text ( ka : kb ), w % cases % part ( t ) == CASE_UPPER ) end if call write_token ( t , text ) end do contains subroutine write_token ( t , text ) !! Write token `t` as `text` (its text with the letter case applied), tracking brackets, !! anchors and trailing comments. integer , intent ( in ) :: t !! index into the token list character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: text !! the text to write if ( tokens % tok ( t )% kind == TK_COMMENT ) then if (. not . w % line_comment ) then ! a trailing comment: later lines may line up with it w % comment_in = input_column ( src , tokens % tok ( t )) w % comment_out = w % col w % line_comment = . true . end if end if if (. not . is_code_kind ( tokens % tok ( t )% kind )) then call put ( w , text ) return end if if ( w % pending_bracket ) w % bracket_first ( w % nbrackets ) = w % col if ( w % pending_anchor > 0 ) w % anchor_col ( w % pending_anchor ) = w % col w % pending_bracket = . false . w % pending_anchor = 0 call put ( w , text ) if ( tokens % tok ( t )% kind == TK_OP ) then select case ( text ) case ( '(' , '[' ) if (. not . allocated ( w % bracket_first )) allocate ( w % bracket_first ( 16 )) if ( w % nbrackets == size ( w % bracket_first )) w % bracket_first = [ w % bracket_first , w % bracket_first ] w % nbrackets = w % nbrackets + 1 w % bracket_first ( w % nbrackets ) = - 1 w % pending_bracket = . true . case ( ')' , ']' ) if ( w % nbrackets > 0 ) w % nbrackets = w % nbrackets - 1 case default if ( w % nbrackets == 0 ) call top_level_operator ( text ) end select end if w % prev = t end subroutine write_token subroutine top_level_operator ( op ) !! Record alignment anchors at a top-level operator. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: op !! text of the operator select case ( op ) case ( '=' , '=>' ) ! an assignment, unless a `,` or `:` came first (`use m, only: a => b`, `integer :: n = 1`), ! or the bindings of `generic :: name => a, b` if (. not . w % separated ) then call anchor ( ANCHOR_ASSIGN ) else if ( op == '=>' . and . w % generic . and . w % declaration ) then call anchor ( ANCHOR_ASSIGN ) end if case ( '::' ) call anchor ( ANCHOR_DECL ) w % separated = . true . w % declaration = . true . case ( ':' ) if ( w % prev > 0 ) then if ( token_lower ( src , tokens % tok ( w % prev )) == 'only' ) call anchor ( ANCHOR_ONLY ) end if w % separated = . true . case ( ',' ) w % separated = . true . end select end subroutine top_level_operator subroutine anchor ( a ) !! Make the next code token the first item after anchor `a`, unless that anchor is already set. integer , intent ( in ) :: a !! `ANCHOR_ASSIGN`, `ANCHOR_ONLY` or `ANCHOR_DECL` if ( w % anchor_col ( a ) < 0 ) w % pending_anchor = a end subroutine anchor end subroutine emit_body","tags":"","url":"proc/emit_body.html"},{"title":"emit_comment_line – fformat","text":"private  subroutine emit_comment_line(w, src, tokens, s, ind, opts) A comment line, re-indented to ind . A comment that lines up with the comment on the line\nabove (a continued trailing comment) stays lined up with it. Comment lines directly after a\nstatement that are indented more than it keep their extra indentation. With keep_column1_comments , a\ncomment that starts in column 1 stays there. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( writer_t ), intent(inout) :: w the output and the alignment state character(len=*), intent(in) :: src the source text type( token_list_t ), intent(in) :: tokens its tokens type( statement_t ), intent(in) :: s the comment line item integer, intent(in) :: ind indentation of the code around it, in blanks type( format_options_t ), intent(in) :: opts the formatting options Calls proc~~emit_comment_line~~CallsGraph proc~emit_comment_line emit_comment_line proc~comment_column comment_column proc~emit_comment_line->proc~comment_column proc~emit_range emit_range proc~emit_comment_line->proc~emit_range proc~input_column input_column proc~emit_comment_line->proc~input_column proc~put put proc~emit_comment_line->proc~put proc~token_text token_text proc~emit_comment_line->proc~token_text proc~trim_blanks trim_blanks proc~emit_comment_line->proc~trim_blanks proc~comment_column->proc~input_column proc~fitting_column fitting_column proc~comment_column->proc~fitting_column proc~emit_range->proc~put proc~emit_range->proc~token_text proc~utf8_width utf8_width proc~input_column->proc~utf8_width proc~builder_append string_builder_t%builder_append proc~put->proc~builder_append proc~put->proc~utf8_width proc~first_piece_width first_piece_width proc~fitting_column->proc~first_piece_width proc~line_width line_width proc~fitting_column->proc~line_width proc~first_piece_width->proc~utf8_width proc~line_pieces line_pieces proc~first_piece_width->proc~line_pieces proc~line_width->proc~utf8_width proc~line_width->proc~line_pieces Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~emit_comment_line~~CalledByGraph proc~emit_comment_line emit_comment_line proc~layout layout proc~layout->proc~emit_comment_line proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~layout proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine emit_comment_line ( w , src , tokens , s , ind , opts ) !! A comment line, re-indented to `ind`. A comment that lines up with the comment on the line !! above (a continued trailing comment) stays lined up with it. Comment lines directly after a !! statement that are indented more than it keep their extra indentation. With `keep_column1_comments`, a !! comment that starts in column 1 stays there. type ( writer_t ), intent ( inout ) :: w !! the output and the alignment state character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: src !! the source text type ( token_list_t ), intent ( in ) :: tokens !! its tokens type ( statement_t ), intent ( in ) :: s !! the comment line item integer , intent ( in ) :: ind !! indentation of the code around it, in blanks type ( format_options_t ), intent ( in ) :: opts !! the formatting options integer :: j , col if (. not . opts % indent_comments ) then call emit_range ( w , src , tokens , s % first , s % last ) w % comment_in = - 1 return end if do j = s % first , s % last select case ( tokens % tok ( j )% kind ) case ( TK_BOM , TK_NEWLINE ) call put ( w , token_text ( src , tokens % tok ( j ))) case ( TK_COMMENT ) if ( opts % keep_column1_comments . and . input_column ( src , tokens % tok ( j )) == 0 ) then col = 0 ! a comment in column 1 stays there w % comment_in = - 1 else col = ind ! comments directly after a statement and indented deeper than it (such as FORD ! `!!` documentation) keep their extra indentation if ( w % stmt_in >= 0 ) col = max ( ind , w % stmt_out + input_column ( src , tokens % tok ( j )) - w % stmt_in ) col = comment_column ( w , src , tokens , j , col ) end if call put ( w , repeat ( ' ' , col )) call put ( w , trim_blanks ( token_text ( src , tokens % tok ( j )))) end select end do end subroutine emit_comment_line","tags":"","url":"proc/emit_comment_line.html"},{"title":"emit_continuation – fformat","text":"private  subroutine emit_continuation(w, src, tokens, f, lend, aligned, indented) A continuation line whose first non-blank token is f , with its code starting at the column aligned , or at indented or its original column if that would make the line too long. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( writer_t ), intent(inout) :: w the output and the alignment state character(len=*), intent(in) :: src the source text type( token_list_t ), intent(in) :: tokens its tokens integer, intent(in) :: f first non-blank token of the line integer, intent(in) :: lend last token of the line, its line break if it has one integer, intent(in) :: aligned preferred column for the code (see continuation_target ) integer, intent(in) :: indented column for the code with a fixed continuation indent Calls proc~~emit_continuation~~CallsGraph proc~emit_continuation emit_continuation proc~emit_body emit_body proc~emit_continuation->proc~emit_body proc~first_non_blank first_non_blank proc~emit_continuation->proc~first_non_blank proc~fitting_column fitting_column proc~emit_continuation->proc~fitting_column proc~input_column input_column proc~emit_continuation->proc~input_column proc~put put proc~emit_continuation->proc~put proc~emit_body->proc~input_column proc~emit_body->proc~put proc~kind_part kind_part proc~emit_body->proc~kind_part proc~line_pieces line_pieces proc~emit_body->proc~line_pieces proc~to_case to_case proc~emit_body->proc~to_case proc~token_lower token_lower proc~emit_body->proc~token_lower proc~first_piece_width first_piece_width proc~fitting_column->proc~first_piece_width proc~line_width line_width proc~fitting_column->proc~line_width proc~utf8_width utf8_width proc~input_column->proc~utf8_width proc~builder_append string_builder_t%builder_append proc~put->proc~builder_append proc~put->proc~utf8_width proc~first_piece_width->proc~line_pieces proc~first_piece_width->proc~utf8_width proc~line_width->proc~line_pieces proc~line_width->proc~utf8_width proc~make_lowercase make_lowercase proc~