lank token is `f`, with its code starting at the column !! `aligned`, or at `indented` or its original column if that would make the line too long. type ( writer_t ), intent ( inout ) :: w !! the output and the alignment state character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: src !! the source text type ( token_list_t ), intent ( in ) :: tokens !! its tokens integer , intent ( in ) :: f !! first non-blank token of the line integer , intent ( in ) :: lend !! last token of the line, its line break if it has one integer , intent ( in ) :: aligned !! preferred column for the code (see [[continuation_target]]) integer , intent ( in ) :: indented !! column for the code with a fixed continuation indent integer :: g , target , orig if ( tokens % tok ( f )% kind /= TK_CONT ) then target = fitting_column ( w , src , tokens , f , lend , [ aligned , indented , input_column ( src , tokens % tok ( f ))]) call put ( w , repeat ( ' ' , target )) call emit_body ( w , src , tokens , f , lend ) return end if ! a leading `&`, placed so that the code after it starts at the target column orig = input_column ( src , tokens % tok ( f )) g = f + 1 if ( g <= lend ) then if ( is_code_kind ( tokens % tok ( g )% kind )) then ! `&code`: keep them together target = fitting_column ( w , src , tokens , f , lend , [ aligned - 1 , indented - 1 , orig ], g , 1 ) call put ( w , repeat ( ' ' , target ) // '&' ) call emit_body ( w , src , tokens , g , lend ) return end if end if g = first_non_blank ( tokens , g , lend ) target = fitting_column ( w , src , tokens , f , lend , [ aligned - 2 , indented - 2 , orig ], g , 2 ) call put ( w , repeat ( ' ' , target ) // '&' ) if ( g <= lend ) then if ( tokens % tok ( g )% kind /= TK_NEWLINE ) call put ( w , ' ' ) end if call emit_body ( w , src , tokens , g , lend ) end subroutine emit_continuation","tags":"","url":"proc/emit_continuation.html"},{"title":"emit_fypp_line – fformat","text":"private  subroutine emit_fypp_line(w, src, tokens, s, ind) A preprocessor line: a fypp directive ( #: , #! , $: , @: ) is indented by ind ; a cpp line\nis written as it is. Continuation lines of the directive are not changed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( writer_t ), intent(inout) :: w the output and the alignment state character(len=*), intent(in) :: src the source text type( token_list_t ), intent(in) :: tokens its tokens type( statement_t ), intent(in) :: s the line, a preprocessor item integer, intent(in) :: ind indentation, in blanks Calls proc~~emit_fypp_line~~CallsGraph proc~emit_fypp_line emit_fypp_line proc~emit_range emit_range proc~emit_fypp_line->proc~emit_range proc~first_non_blank first_non_blank proc~emit_fypp_line->proc~first_non_blank proc~put put proc~emit_fypp_line->proc~put proc~emit_range->proc~put proc~token_text token_text proc~emit_range->proc~token_text proc~builder_append string_builder_t%builder_append proc~put->proc~builder_append proc~utf8_width utf8_width proc~put->proc~utf8_width Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~emit_fypp_line~~CalledByGraph proc~emit_fypp_line emit_fypp_line proc~layout layout proc~layout->proc~emit_fypp_line proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~layout proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_