tement label integer, intent(in) :: ind indentation of the statement, in blanks type( format_options_t ), intent(in) :: opts the formatting options Calls proc~~emit_statement~~CallsGraph proc~emit_statement emit_statement proc~comment_column comment_column proc~emit_statement->proc~comment_column proc~continuation_target continuation_target proc~emit_statement->proc~continuation_target proc~emit_body emit_body proc~emit_statement->proc~emit_body proc~emit_continuation emit_continuation proc~emit_statement->proc~emit_continuation proc~emit_range emit_range proc~emit_statement->proc~emit_range proc~first_non_blank first_non_blank proc~emit_statement->proc~first_non_blank proc~fitting_column fitting_column proc~emit_statement->proc~fitting_column proc~input_column input_column proc~emit_statement->proc~input_column proc~put put proc~emit_statement->proc~put proc~token_lower token_lower proc~emit_statement->proc~token_lower proc~token_text token_text proc~emit_statement->proc~token_text proc~comment_column->proc~fitting_column proc~comment_column->proc~input_column proc~emit_body->proc~input_column proc~emit_body->proc~put proc~emit_body->proc~token_lower proc~kind_part kind_part proc~emit_body->proc~kind_part proc~line_pieces line_pieces proc~emit_body->proc~line_pieces proc~to_case to_case proc~emit_body->proc~to_case proc~emit_continuation->proc~emit_body proc~emit_continuation->proc~first_non_blank proc~emit_continuation->proc~fitting_column proc~emit_continuation->proc~input_column proc~emit_continuation->proc~put proc~emit_range->proc~put proc~emit_range->proc~token_text proc~first_piece_width first_piece_width proc~fitting_column->proc~first_piece_width proc~line_width line_width proc~fitting_column->proc~line_width proc~utf8_width utf8_width proc~input_column->proc~utf8_width proc~builder_append string_builder_t%builder_append proc~put->proc~builder_append proc~put->proc~utf8_width proc~make_lowercase make_lowercase proc~token_lower->proc~make_lowercase proc~first_piece_width->proc~line_pieces proc~first_piece_width->proc~utf8_width proc~line_width->proc~line_pieces proc~line_width->proc~utf8_width Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~emit_statement~~CalledByGraph proc~emit_statement emit_statement proc~layout layout proc~layout->proc~emit_statement proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~layout proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine emit_statement ( w , src , tokens , s , labeled , ind , opts ) !! A code statement, with its continuation lines and the comment, blank and preprocessor lines !! between them. The first line is indented to `ind`; a statement label stays at the start of !! the line. type ( writer_t ), intent ( inout ) :: w !! the output and the alignment state character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: src !! the source text type ( token_list_t ), intent ( in ) :: tokens !! its tokens type ( statement_t ), intent ( in ) :: s !! the code statement logical , intent ( in ) :: labeled !! the statement has a statement label integer , intent ( in ) :: ind !! indentation of the statement, in blanks type ( format_options_t ), intent ( in ) :: opts !! the formatting options integer :: j , lend , f logical :: first_line , mid_line w % nbrackets = 0 w % anchor_col = - 1 w % pending_anchor = 0 w % pending_bracket = . false . w % separated = . false . w % declaration = . false . w % prev = 0 ! a statement after `;` starts in the middle of a line mid_line = . false . if ( s % first > 1 ) mid_line = tokens % tok ( s % first - 1 )% kind /= TK_NEWLINE . and . tokens % tok ( s % first - 1 )% kind /= TK_BOM first_line = . true . j = s % first do while ( j <= s % last ) lend = j do while ( lend < s % last ) if ( tokens % tok ( lend )% kind == TK_NEWLINE ) exit lend = lend + 1 end do if ( tokens % tok ( j )% kind == TK_BOM ) then call put ( w , token_text ( src , tokens % tok ( j ))) j = j + 1 end if f = first_non_blank ( tokens , j , lend ) w % line_comment = . false . if ( f > lend ) then continue ! nothing left on the line else if ( tokens % tok ( f )% kind == TK_NEWLINE ) then call put ( w , token_text ( src , tokens % tok ( f ))) ! blank line else if ( tokens % tok ( f )% kind == TK_PREPROC ) then call emit_range ( w , src , tokens , j , lend ) else if ( tokens % tok ( f )% kind == TK_COMMENT ) then call put ( w , repeat ( ' ' , comment_column ( w , src , tokens , f , ind + opts % continuation_indent ))) call emit_body ( w , src , tokens , f , lend ) w % line_comment = . true . else if ( first_line ) then if ( mid_line ) then call emit_body ( w , src , tokens , j , lend ) else if ( labeled . and . tokens % tok ( f )% kind == TK_INT ) then call put ( w , token_text ( src , tokens % tok ( f ))) call put ( w , repeat ( ' ' , max ( 1 , ind - w % col ))) call start_statement ( first_non_blank ( tokens , f + 1 , lend )) ! the code after the label call emit_body ( w , src , tokens , first_non_blank ( tokens , f + 1 , lend ), lend ) else call put ( w , repeat ( ' ' , fitting_column ( w , src , tokens , f , lend , & [ ind , input_column ( src , tokens % tok ( f ))]))) call start_statement ( f ) call emit_body ( w , src , tokens , f , lend ) end if first_line = . false . else call emit_continuation ( w , src , tokens , f , lend , continuation_target ( w , ind , opts ), & ind + opts % continuation_indent ) end if if (. not . w % line_comment ) w % comment_in = - 1 w % pending_anchor = 0 w % pending_bracket = . false . j = lend + 1 end do contains subroutine start_statement ( f ) !! Record where the statement starting with token `f` begins, for comment lines after it. integer , intent ( in ) :: f !! first code token of the statement, after any label w % stmt_in = - 1 if ( f > s % last ) return w % stmt_in = input_column ( src , tokens % tok ( f )) w % stmt_out = w % col w % generic = token_lower ( src , tokens % tok ( f )) == 'generic' end subroutine start_statement end subroutine emit_statement","tags":"","url":"proc/emit_statement.html"},{"title":"line_pieces – fformat","text":"private  subroutine line_pieces(w, src, tokens, first, lend, pieces) The pieces of output for tokens first:lend of a line: the tokens, with the blanks between them\nadjusted by the whitespace rules and trailing blanks removed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( writer_t ), intent(in) :: w the output and the alignment state character(len=*), intent(in) :: src the source text type( token_list_t ), intent(in) :: tokens its tokens integer, intent(in) :: first first token of the part of the line integer, intent(in) :: lend last token of the line, its line break if it has one type( piece_t ), intent(out), allocatable :: pieces (:) the pieces, in order Called by proc~~line_pieces~~CalledByGraph proc~line_pieces line_pieces proc~emit_body emit_body proc~emit_body->proc~line_pieces proc~first_piece_width first_piece_width proc~first_piece_width->proc~line_pieces proc~line_width line_width proc~line_width->proc~line_pieces proc~emit_continuation emit_continuation proc~emit_continuation->proc~emit_body proc~fitting_column fitting_column proc~emit_continuation->proc~fitting_column proc~emit_statement emit_statement proc~emit_statement->proc~emit_body proc~emit_statement->proc~emit_continuation proc~emit_statement->proc~fitting_column proc~comment_column comment_column proc~emit_statement->proc~comment_column proc~fitting_column->proc~first_piece_width proc~fitting_column->proc~line_width proc~comment_column->proc~fitting_column proc~layout layout proc~layout->proc~emit_statement proc~emit_comment_line emit_comment_line proc~layout->proc~emit_comment_line proc~emit_comment_line->proc~comment_column proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~layout proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine line_pieces ( w , src , tokens , first , lend , pieces ) !! The pieces of output for tokens `first:lend` of a line: the tokens, with the blanks between them !! adjusted by the whitespace rules and trailing blanks removed. type ( writer_t ), intent ( in ) :: w !! the output and the alignment state character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: src !! the source text type ( token_list_t ), intent ( in ) :: tokens !! its tokens integer , intent ( in ) :: first !! first token of the part of the line integer , intent ( in ) :: lend !! last token of the line, its line break if it has one type ( piece_t ), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: pieces (:) !! the pieces, in order integer :: t , n , g , last allocate ( pieces ( 2 * ( lend - first + 1 ) + 1 )) n = 0 do t = first , lend if ( tokens % tok ( t )% kind == TK_SPACE ) then if ( t == lend ) cycle if ( tokens % tok ( t + 1 )% kind == TK_NEWLINE ) cycle g = - 1 ! blanks between two code tokens may be adjusted by the rule for the second one, and ! blanks before a trailing comment by the comment spacing if ( t > first . and . t < lend ) then if ( is_code_kind ( tokens % tok ( t - 1 )% kind ) . and . is_code_kind ( tokens % tok ( t + 1 )% kind )) then g = w % gap ( t + 1 ) else if ( tokens % tok ( t + 1 )% kind == TK_COMMENT ) then g = w % gap ( t + 1 ) end if if ( g == 0 ) cycle end if call add ( 0 , tokens % tok ( t )% first , tokens % tok ( t )% last , max ( g , 0 )) cycle end if if ( t > first ) then if ( is_code_kind ( tokens % tok ( t )% kind ) . and . is_code_kind ( tokens % tok ( t - 1 )% kind )) then g = w % gap ( t ) ! no blank in the input if ( g == GAP_MIN1 ) then call add ( 0 , 1 , 0 , 1 ) else if ( g > 0 ) then call add ( 0 , 1 , 0 , g ) end if else if ( tokens % tok ( t )% kind == TK_COMMENT . and . tokens % tok ( t - 1 )% kind /= TK_SPACE ) then if ( w % gap ( t ) > 0 ) call add ( 0 , 1 , 0 , w % gap ( t )) ! a trailing comment right after the code end if end if last = tokens % tok ( t )% last if ( tokens % tok ( t )% kind == TK_COMMENT ) then ! without trailing blanks and tabs do while ( last >= tokens % tok ( t )% first ) if ( src ( last : last ) /= ' ' . and . src ( last : last ) /= achar ( 9 )) exit last = last - 1 end do end if call add ( t , tokens % tok ( t )% first , last , 0 ) end do pieces = pieces ( 1 : n ) contains subroutine add ( tok , from , to , blanks ) !! Append a piece with these components (see [[piece_t]]). integer , intent ( in ) :: tok , from , to , blanks !! its `tok`, `first`, `last` and `blanks` n = n + 1 pieces ( n ) = piece_t ( tok , from , to , blanks ) end subroutine add end subroutine line_pieces","tags":"","url":"proc/line_pieces.html"},{"title":"put – fformat","text":"private  subroutine put(w, text) Append text and track the output column. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( writer_t ), intent(inout) :: w the output and the alignment state character(len=*), intent(in) :: text text to append; it may contain line breaks Calls proc~~put~~CallsGraph proc~put put proc~builder_append string_builder_t%builder_append proc~put->proc~builder_append proc~utf8_width utf8_width proc~put->proc~utf8_width Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~put~~CalledByGraph proc~put put proc~emit_blank emit_blank proc~emit_b