y This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code logical function is_directory ( path ) !! True if `path` is a directory (or a link to one): if it can be opened as a directory. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path !! the path to test type ( c_ptr ) :: dir integer :: status dir = c_opendir ( c_string ( path )) is_directory = c_associated ( dir ) if ( is_directory ) status = c_closedir ( dir ) end function is_directory","tags":"","url":"proc/is_directory.html"},{"title":"join_path – fformat","text":"public pure function join_path(dir, name) result(path) dir/name , without doubling a separator. A trailing \\ or : (Windows) also counts. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: dir the directory, and the name to append to it character(len=*), intent(in) :: name the directory, and the name to append to it Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Called by proc~~join_path~~CalledByGraph proc~join_path join_path proc~absolute_path absolute_path proc~absolute_path->proc~join_path proc~child child proc~child->proc~join_path proc~find_config find_config proc~find_config->proc~join_path proc~list_directory list_directory proc~list_directory->proc~join_path proc~collect_files collect_files proc~collect_files->proc~child proc~collect_files->proc~list_directory proc~config_for config_for proc~config_for->proc~find_config proc~directory_files directory_files proc~directory_files->proc~absolute_path proc~directory_files->proc~collect_files proc~directory_files->proc~config_for proc~options_for options_for proc~options_for->proc~absolute_path proc~options_for->proc~config_for proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~absolute_path proc~process_text process_text 