hich implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code function default_extensions () result ( list ) !! Extensions of free-form Fortran files. type ( string_t ), allocatable :: list (:) list = [ string_t ( 'f90' ), string_t ( 'F90' ), string_t ( 'f95' ), string_t ( 'F95' ), string_t ( 'f03' ), & string_t ( 'F03' ), string_t ( 'f08' ), string_t ( 'F08' ), string_t ( 'f18' ), string_t ( 'F18' )] end function default_extensions","tags":"","url":"proc/default_extensions.html"},{"title":"glob_to_regex – fformat","text":"public  function glob_to_regex(glob) result(re) A regular expression (for a full match) equivalent to the glob pattern glob . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: glob the glob pattern Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Calls proc~~glob_to_regex~~CallsGraph proc~glob_to_regex glob_to_regex re_escape re_escape proc~glob_to_regex->re_escape Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~glob_to_regex~~CalledByGraph proc~glob_to_regex glob_to_regex proc~collect_files collect_files proc~collect_files->proc~glob_to_regex proc~directory_files directory_files proc~directory_files->proc~collect_files proc~run run proc~run->proc~directory_files Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code function glob_to_regex ( glob ) result ( re ) !! A regular expression (for a full match) equivalent to the glob pattern `glob`. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: glob !! the glob pattern character ( len = :), allocatable :: re integer :: i , j re = '' i = 1 do while ( i <= len ( glob )) select case ( glob ( i : i )) case ( '*' ) if ( i < len ( glob )) then if ( glob ( i + 1 : i + 1 ) == '*' ) then if ( i + 1 < len ( glob )) then if ( glob ( i + 2 : i + 2 ) == '/' ) then re = re // '(?:.*/)?' ! `**/`: any number of directories i = i + 3 cycle end if end if re = re // '.*' i = i + 2 cycle end if end if re = re // '[&#94;/]*' case ( '?' ) re = re // '[&#94;/]' case ( '[' ) j = index ( glob ( i + 1 :), ']' ) if ( j > 1 ) then if ( glob ( i + 1 : i + 1 ) == '!' ) then re = re // '[&#94;' // glob ( i + 2 : i + j ) else re = re // glob ( i : i + j ) end if i = i + j + 1 cycle end if re = re // '' case default re = re // re_escape ( glob ( i : i )) end select i = i + 1 end do end function glob_to_regex","tags":"","url":"proc/glob_to_regex.html"},{"title":"collect_files – fformat","text":"public  subroutine collect_files(root, extensions, exclude, files) The files under directory root with one of the extensions (without the dot) that are not\nexcluded, sorted by path within each directory. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: root the directory to search type( string_t ), intent(in) :: extensions (:) extensions of the files to collect, without the dot type( string_t ), intent(in) :: exclude (:) glob patterns of the files and directories to skip type( string_t ), intent(out), allocatable :: files (:) paths of the files, root joined with their\nrelative paths (just those if root is . ) Calls proc~~collect_files~~CallsGraph proc~collect_files collect_files fullmatch fullmatch proc~collect_files->fullmatch proc~child child proc~collect_files->proc~child proc~glob_to_regex glob_to_regex proc~collect_files->proc~glob_to_regex proc~list_directory list_directory proc~collect_files->proc~list_directory proc~sort_entries sort_entries proc~collect_files->proc~sort_entries regex regex proc~collect_files->regex proc~join_path join_path proc~child->proc~join_path re_escape re_escape proc~glob_to_regex->re_escape interface~c_closedir c_closedir proc~list_directory->interface~c_closedir interface~c_opendir c_opendir proc~list_directory->interface~c_opendir interface~c_readdir c_readdir proc~list_directory->interface~c_readdir proc~byte_at byte_at proc~list_directory->proc~byte_at proc~c_string c_string proc~list_directory->proc~c_string proc~entry_name entry_name proc~list_directory->proc~entry_name proc~find_layout find_layout proc~list_directory->proc~find_layout proc~is_directory is_directory proc~list_directory->proc~is_directory proc~list_directory->proc~join_path proc~find_layout->interface~c_closedir proc~find_layout->interface~c_opendir proc~find_layout->interface~c_readdir proc~find_layout->proc~byte_at proc~find_layout->proc~c_string proc~is_directory->interface~c_closedir proc~is_directory->interface~c_opendir proc~is_directory->proc~c_string Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~collect_files~~CalledByGraph proc~collect_files collect_files proc~directory_files directory_files proc~directory_files->proc~collect_files proc~run run proc~run->proc~directory_files Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine collect_files ( root , extensions , exclude , files ) !! The files under directory `root` with one of the `extensions` (without the dot) that are not !! excluded, sorted by path within each directory. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: root !! the directory to search type ( string_t ), intent ( in ) :: extensions (:) !! extensions of the files to collect, without the dot type ( string_t ), intent ( in ) :: exclude (:) !! glob patterns of the files and directories to skip type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: files (:) !! paths of the files, `root` joined with their !! relative paths (just those if `root` is `.`) type ( regex_t ), allocatable :: patterns (:) logical , allocatable :: by_path (:) integer :: k allocate ( files ( 0 ), patterns ( size ( exclude )), by_path ( size ( exclude ))) do k = 1 , size ( exclude ) patterns ( k ) = regex ( glob_to_regex ( exclude ( k )% s )) by_path ( k ) = index ( exclude ( k )% s , '/' ) > 0 end do call walk ( root , '' , 0 ) contains recursive subroutine walk ( dir , rel , depth ) !! Add the files under directory `dir` to `files`, descending at most `MAX_DEPTH` levels. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: dir !! the directory's path character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: rel !! its path relative to `root` (`''` for `root`) integer , intent ( in ) :: depth !! its depth below `root` type ( dir_entry_t ), allocatable :: entries (:) character ( len = :), allocatable :: rel_path , path integer :: k , stat if ( depth > MAX_DEPTH ) return call list_directory ( dir , entries , stat ) if ( stat /= 0 ) return call sort_entries ( entries ) do k = 1 , size ( entries ) if ( len ( rel ) == 0 ) then rel_path = entries ( k )% name else rel_path = rel // '/' // entries ( k )% name end if if ( excluded ( entries ( k )% name , rel_path )) cycle path = child ( dir , entries ( k )% name ) select case ( entries ( k )% kind ) case ( ENTRY_DIR ) call walk ( path , rel_path , depth + 1 ) case ( ENTRY_FILE ) if ( has_extension ( entries ( k )% name )) files = [ files , string_t ( path )] end select end do end subroutine walk logical function excluded ( name , rel_path ) !! True if an exclude pattern matches the entry: its `name`, or its `rel_path` for a !! pattern with a `/`. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! the entry's name character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: rel_path !! its path relative to `root` integer :: k excluded = . false . do k = 1 , size ( patterns ) if ( by_path ( k )) then excluded = patterns ( k )% fullmatch ( rel_path ) else excluded = patterns ( k )% fullmatch ( name ) end if if ( excluded ) return end do end function excluded logical function has_extension ( name ) !! True if file name `name` ends with `.` and one of the `extensions`, after at least one !! other character. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! the file name integer :: k , n has_extension = . false . do k = 1 , size ( extensions ) n = len ( extensions ( k )% s ) + 1 if ( len ( name ) > n ) then if ( name ( len ( name ) - n + 1 :) == '.' // extensions ( k )% s ) then has_extension = . true . return end if end if end do end function has_extension end subroutine collect_files","tags":"","url":"proc/collect_files.html"},{"title":"sort_entries – fformat","text":"private  subroutine sort_entries(entries) Sort by name (insertion sort: directories are small). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( dir_entry_t ), intent(inout) :: entries (:) a directory listing Called by proc~~sort_entries~~CalledByGraph proc~sort_entries sort_entries proc~collect_files collect_files proc~collect_files->proc~sort_entries proc~directory_files directory_files proc~directory_files->proc~collect_files proc~run run proc~run->proc~directory_files Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine sort_entries ( entries ) !! Sort by name (insertion sort: directories are small). type ( dir_entry_t ), intent ( inout ) :: entries (:) !! a directory listing type ( dir_entry_t ) :: e integer :: i , j do i = 2 , size ( entries ) e = entries ( i ) j = i - 1 do while ( j >= 1 ) if (. not . llt ( e % name , entries ( j )% name )) exit entries ( j + 1 ) = entries ( j ) j = j - 1 end do entries ( j + 1 ) = e end do end subroutine sort_entries","tags":"","url":"proc/sort_entries.html"},{"title":"classify_statement – fformat","text":"public  function classify_statement(src, tokens, v, in_interface) result(info) Classify a code statement. in_interface is true directly inside an interface block,\nwhere module procedure lists procedures instead of starting one. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: src source text type( token_list_t ), intent(in) :: tokens tokens of src type( statement_view_t ), intent(in) :: v the statement logical, intent(in) :: in_interface the innermost open construct is an interface block Return Value type( stmt_info_t ) Calls proc~~classify_statement~~CallsGraph proc~classify_statement classify_statement proc~closed_construct closed_construct proc~classify_statement->proc~closed_construct proc~expand_keyword expand_keyword proc~classify_statement->proc~expand_keyword proc~set set proc~classify_statement->proc~set proc~view_closing statement_view_t%view_closing proc~classify_statement->proc~view_closing proc~view_kind_of statement_view_t%view_kind_of proc~classify_statement->proc~view_kind_of proc~view_word statement_view_t%view_word proc~classify_statement->proc~view_word Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~classify_statement~~CalledByGraph proc~classify_statement classify_statement proc~analyze_structure analyze_structure proc~analyze_structure->proc~classify_statement proc~format_pass format_pass proc~format_pass->proc~analyze_structure proc~format_text format_text proc~format_text->proc~format_pass proc~relayout relayout proc~format_text->proc~relayout proc~relayout->proc~format_pass proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~format_text proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~proces