edure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure function lcs_lengths ( a , b ) result ( row ) !! `row(k)`: the length of the longest common subsequence of `a` and `b(1:k)`. integer , intent ( in ) :: a (:), b (:) !! line numbers of the two texts integer :: row ( 0 : size ( b )) integer :: prev ( 0 : size ( b )) integer :: i , k row = 0 do i = 1 , size ( a ) prev = row do k = 1 , size ( b ) if ( a ( i ) == b ( k )) then row ( k ) = prev ( k - 1 ) + 1 else row ( k ) = max ( row ( k - 1 ), prev ( k )) end if end do end do end function lcs_lengths","tags":"","url":"proc/lcs_lengths.html"},{"title":"range_text – fformat","text":"private pure function range_text(start, n) result(text) start,n for a hunk header; start is the line before the hunk when it is empty. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: start first line of the hunk integer, intent(in) :: n number of lines in the hunk Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Calls proc~~range_text~~CallsGraph proc~range_text range_text proc~to_s to_s proc~range_text->proc~to_s Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~range_text~~CalledByGraph proc~range_text range_text proc~unified_diff unified_diff proc~unified_diff->proc~range_text proc~process_