unified_diff proc~builder_append string_builder_t%builder_append proc~unified_diff->proc~builder_append proc~builder_get string_builder_t%builder_get proc~unified_diff->proc~builder_get proc~lcs lcs proc~unified_diff->proc~lcs proc~line_ids line_ids proc~unified_diff->proc~line_ids proc~range_text range_text proc~unified_diff->proc~range_text proc~split_lines split_lines proc~unified_diff->proc~split_lines proc~lcs->proc~lcs proc~lcs_lengths lcs_lengths proc~lcs->proc~lcs_lengths proc~hash hash proc~line_ids->proc~hash proc~to_s to_s proc~range_text->proc~to_s Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~unified_diff~~CalledByGraph proc~unified_diff unified_diff proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~unified_diff proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code function unified_diff ( a , b , name , context ) result ( diff ) !! The changes from `a` to `b` as a unified diff with `context` lines of context (default 3), !! with `name` in the headers. Empty if the texts are equal. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: a !! the old text character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: b !! the new text character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! file name for the `---` and `+++` headers integer , intent ( in ), optional :: context !! number of unchanged lines shown around each change character ( len = :), allocatable :: diff type ( string_t ), allocatable :: la (:), lb (:) integer , allocatable :: ia (:), ib (:) type ( edit_t ) :: e type ( string_builder_t ) :: buf integer :: ctx , k , first , last , i , j , ka , kb , na , nb , start_a , start_b diff = '' if ( a == b . and . len ( a ) == len ( b )) return ctx = 3 if ( present ( context )) ctx = context la = split_lines ( a ) lb = split_lines ( b ) call line_ids ( la , lb , ia , ib ) allocate ( e % op ( size ( ia ) + size ( ib ))) call lcs ( ia , 1 , size ( ia ), ib , 1 , size ( ib ), e ) call buf % append ( '--- ' // name // new_line ( 'a' ) // '+++ ' // name // new_line ( 'a' )) ! hunks: runs of edits with at most 2*ctx equal lines between them, plus context around k = 1 i = 1 ! next line of a j = 1 ! next line of b do while ( k <= e % n ) if ( e % op ( k ) == OP_EQUAL ) then k = k + 1 i = i + 1 j = j + 1 cycle end if first = k last = k do while ( last < e % n ) ! extend over changes separated by short runs of equal lines ka = last + 1 do while ( ka <= e % n ) if ( e % op ( ka ) /= OP_EQUAL ) exit ka = ka + 1 end do if ( ka > e % n . or . ka - last - 1 > 2 * ctx ) exit last = ka end do ! the hunk covers edits first-ctx .. last+ctx (equal lines at both ends) ka = first nb = 0 do while ( ka > 1 . and . nb < ctx ) if ( e % op ( ka - 1 ) /= OP_EQUAL ) exit ka = ka - 1 nb = nb + 1 end do start_a = i - nb start_b = j - nb kb = last nb = 0 do while ( kb < e % n . and . nb < ctx ) if ( e % op ( kb + 1 ) /= OP_EQUAL ) exit kb = kb + 1 nb = nb + 1 end do na = count ( e % op ( ka : kb ) /= OP_INSERT ) nb = count ( e % op ( ka : kb ) /= OP_DELETE ) call buf % append ( '@@ -' // range_text ( start_a , na ) // ' +' // range_text ( start_b , nb ) // ' @@' // new_line ( 'a' )) i = start_a j = start_b do k = ka , kb select case ( e % op ( k )) case ( OP_EQUAL ) call add_line ( ' ' , la ( i )% s ) i = i + 1 j = j + 1 case ( OP_DELETE ) call add_line ( '-' , la ( i )% s ) i = i + 1 case ( OP_INSERT ) call add_line ( '+' , lb ( j )% s ) j = j + 1 end select end do k = kb + 1 end do diff = buf % get () contains subroutine add_line ( mark , line ) !! Append `line` to the diff after `mark`, with a \"No newline\" note if it has no line ending. character , intent ( in ) :: mark !! ` ` for context, `-` for a deleted line, `+` for an inserted one character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: line !! the line, with its line ending call buf % append ( mark // line ) if ( len ( line ) == 0 ) then call buf % append ( new_line ( 'a' ) // '\\ No newline at end of file' // new_line ( 'a' )) else if ( line ( len ( line ): len ( line )) /= achar ( 10 )) then call buf % append ( new_line ( 'a' ) // '\\ No newline at end of file' // new_line ( 'a' )) end if end subroutine add_line end function unified_diff","tags":"","url":"proc/unified_diff.html"},{"title":"lcs – fformat","text":"private recursive subroutine lcs(a, a0, a1, b, b0, b1, e) Append the edits that turn a(a0:a1) into b(b0:b1) along a longest common subsequence\n(Hirschberg's algorithm). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: a (:) line numbers of the two texts, from line_ids integer, intent(in) :: a0 the ranges of a and b to compare integer, intent(in) :: a1 the ranges of a and b to compare integer, intent(in) :: b (:) line numbers of the two texts, from line_ids integer, intent(in) :: b0 the ranges of a and b to compare integer, intent(in) :: b1 the ranges of a and b to compare type( edit_t ), intent(inout) :: e the edits so far; e%op must have room for the new ones Calls proc~~lcs~~CallsGraph proc~lcs lcs proc~lcs->proc~lcs proc~lcs_lengths lcs_lengths proc~lcs->proc~lcs_lengths Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~lcs~~CalledByGraph proc~lcs lcs proc~lcs->proc~lcs proc~unified_diff unified_diff proc~unified_diff->proc~lcs proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~unified_diff proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code recursive subroutine lcs ( a , a0 , a1 , b , b0 , b1 , e ) !! Append the edits that turn `a(a0:a1)` into `b(b0:b1)` along a longest common subsequence !! (Hirschberg's algorithm). integer , intent ( in ) :: a (:), b (:) !! line numbers of the two texts, from `line_ids` integer , intent ( in ) :: a0 , a1 , b0 , b1 !! the ranges of `a` and `b` to compare type ( edit_t ), intent ( inout ) :: e !! the edits so far; `e%op` must have room for the new ones integer :: lo_a , lo_b , hi_a , hi_b , nsuffix , k ! common prefix and suffix, without recursion lo_a = a0 lo_b = b0 do while ( lo_a <= a1 . and . lo_b <= b1 ) if ( a ( lo_a ) /= b ( lo_b )) exit call push ( OP_EQUAL ) lo_a = lo_a + 1 lo_b = lo_b + 1 end do hi_a = a1 hi_b = b1 nsuffix = 0 do while ( hi_a >= lo_a . and . hi_b >= lo_b ) if ( a ( hi_a ) /= b ( hi_b )) exit hi_a = hi_a - 1 hi_b = hi_b - 1 nsuffix = nsuffix + 1 end do call middle ( lo_a , hi_a , lo_b , hi_b ) do k = 1 , nsuffix call push ( OP_EQUAL ) end do contains recursive subroutine middle ( a0 , a1 , b0 , b1 ) !! The edits for `a(a0:a1)` and `b(b0:b1)`, which differ at both ends. integer , intent ( in ) :: a0 , a1 , b0 , b1 !! the ranges of `a` and `b` integer :: fwd ( 0 : b1 - b0 + 1 ), bwd ( 0 : b1 - b0 + 1 ) ! (not allocatable: assignment would make them 1-based) integer :: mid , k , best , split , j if ( a0 > a1 ) then do j = b0 , b1 call push ( OP_INSERT ) end do return end if if ( b0 > b1 ) then do j = a0 , a1 call push ( OP_DELETE ) end do return end if if ( a0 == a1 ) then ! one line of a: keep it if it occurs in b do j = b0 , b1 if ( b ( j ) == a ( a0 )) then do k = b0 , j - 1 call push ( OP_INSERT ) end do call push ( OP_EQUAL ) do k = j + 1 , b1 call push ( OP_INSERT ) end do return end if end do call push ( OP_DELETE ) do k = b0 , b1 call push ( OP_INSERT ) end do return end if mid = ( a0 + a1 ) / 2 fwd = lcs_lengths ( a ( a0 : mid ), b ( b0 : b1 )) bwd = lcs_lengths ( a ( a1 : mid + 1 : - 1 ), b ( b1 : b0 : - 1 )) best = - 1 split = 0 do k = 0 , b1 - b0 + 1 if ( fwd ( k ) + bwd ( b1 - b0 + 1 - k ) > best ) then best = fwd ( k ) + bwd ( b1 - b0 + 1 - k ) split = k end if end do call lcs ( a , a0 , mid , b , b0 , b0 + split - 1 , e ) call lcs ( a , mid + 1 , a1 , b , b0 + split , b1 , e ) end subroutine middle subroutine push ( op ) !! Append edit `op` (`OP_EQUAL`, `OP_DELETE` or `OP_INSERT`) to `e`. integer , intent ( in ) :: op !! the edit e % n = e % n + 1 e % op ( e % n ) = op end subroutine push end subroutine lcs","tags":"","url":"proc/lcs.html"},{"title":"line_ids – fformat","text":"private  subroutine line_ids(la, lb, ia, ib) Number the distinct lines, so that equal lines have equal numbers. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( string_t ), intent(in) :: la (:) the lines of the two texts type( string_t ), intent(in) :: lb (:) the lines of the two texts integer, intent(out), allocatable :: ia (:) the number of each line of la and lb integer, intent(out), allocatable :: ib (:) the number of each line of la and lb Calls proc~~line_ids~~CallsGraph proc~line_ids line_ids proc~hash hash proc~line_ids->proc~hash Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~line_ids~~CalledByGraph proc~line_ids line_ids proc~unified_diff unified_diff proc~unified_diff->proc~line_ids proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~unified_diff proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine line_ids ( la , lb , ia , ib ) !! Number the distinct lines, so that equal lines have equal numbers. type ( string_t ), intent ( in ) :: la (:), lb (:) !! the lines of the two texts integer , allocatable , intent ( out ) :: ia (:), ib (:) !! the number of each line of `la` and `lb` integer , allocatable :: slot (:) ! hash table: id of the line in each slot, or 0 type ( string_t ), allocatable :: seen (:) integer :: k , nseen , mask mask = 1 do while ( mask < 2 * ( size ( la ) + size ( lb )) + 1 ) mask = 2 * mask end do allocate ( slot ( 0 : mask - 1 ), seen ( size ( la ) + size ( lb )), ia ( size ( la )), ib ( size ( lb ))) mask = mask - 1 slot = 0 nseen = 0 do k = 1 , size ( la ) ia ( k ) = id_of ( la ( k )% s ) end do do k = 1 , size ( lb ) ib ( k ) = id_of ( lb ( k )% s ) end do contains integer function id_of ( line ) !! The number of `line`: that of an equal line seen before, or the next new number. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: line !! a line of `la` or `lb` integer :: h h = int ( iand ( hash ( line ), int ( mask , int64 ))) do if ( slot ( h ) == 0 ) then nseen = nseen + 1 seen ( nseen )% s = line slot ( h ) = nseen id_of = nseen return end if if ( len ( seen ( slot ( h ))% s ) == len ( line )) then if ( seen ( slot ( h ))% s == line ) then id_of = slot ( h ) return end if end if h = iand ( h + 1 , mask ) end do end function id_of end subroutine line_ids","tags":"","url":"proc/line_ids.html"},{"title":"apply_setting – fformat","text":"public  subroutine apply_setting(opts, key, value, stat, errmsg) Apply one setting to opts . stat is nonzero, with a message, for an unknown setting or a bad value. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( format_options_t ), intent(inout) :: opts the options to change character(len=*), intent(in) :: key setting name, as in the table above character(len=*), intent(in) :: value its value as text integer, intent(out) :: stat 0, or 1 for an unknown setting or a bad value character(len=:), intent(out), allocatable :: errmsg what is wrong, if stat is nonzero Calls proc~~apply_setting~~CallsGraph proc~apply_setting apply_setting proc~to_s to_s proc~apply_setting->proc~to_s Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~apply_setting~~CalledByGraph proc~apply_setting apply_setting proc~options_for options_for proc~options_for->proc~apply_setting proc~parse_args parse_args proc~parse_args->proc~apply_setting proc~process_text process_text proc~process_text->proc~options_for proc~process_file process_file proc~process_file->proc~process_text proc~process_stdin process_stdin proc~process_stdin->proc~process_text proc~run run proc~run->proc~process_file proc~run->proc~process_stdin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine apply_setting ( opts , key , value , stat , errmsg ) !! Apply one setting to `opts`. `stat` is nonzero, with a message, for an unknown setting or a bad value. type ( format_options_t ), intent ( inout ) :: opts !! the options to change character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: key !! setting name, as in the table above character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: value !! its value as text integer , intent ( out ) :: stat !! 0, or 1 for an unknown setting or a bad value character ( len = :), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: errmsg !! what is wrong, if `stat` is nonzero stat = 0 select case ( key ) case ( 'indent' ) call read_count ( 64 , opts % indent ) case ( 'base-indent' ) call read_count ( 64 , opts % base_indent ) case ( 'continuation-indent' ) call read_count ( 64 , opts % continuation_indent ) case ( 'line-length' ) call read_count ( 100000 , opts % line_length ) case ( 'indent-units' ) call read_flag ( opts % indent_units ) case ( 'indent-procedures' ) call read_flag ( opts % indent_procedures ) case ( 'indent-fypp' ) call read_flag ( opts % indent_fypp ) case ( 'indent-comments' ) call read_flag ( opts % indent_comments ) case ( 'column1-comments' ) select case ( value ) case ( 'keep' ) opts % keep_column1_comments = . true . case ( 'indent' ) opts % keep_column1_comments = . false . case default call fail ( '\"keep\" or \"indent\"' ) end select case ( 'split' ) call read_flag ( opts % split_lines ) case ( 'sort-use' ) call read_flag ( opts % sort_use ) case ( 'sort-use-only' ) call read_flag ( opts % sort_use_only ) case ( 'comment-spacing' ) if ( value == 'keep' ) then opts % comment_spacing = - 1 else call read_count ( 64 , opts % comment_spacing ) if ( stat /= 0 ) errmsg = 'expected a number from 0 to 64 or keep for \"' // key // '\", not \"' // value // '\"' end if case ( 'continuation' ) select case ( value ) case ( 'align' ) opts % continuation = CONT_ALIGN case ( 'indent' ) opts % continuation = CONT_INDENT case default call fail ( '\"align\" or \"indent\"' ) end select case ( 'relational' ) select case ( value ) case ( 'symbols' ) opts % relational = REL_SYMBOLS case ( 'letters' ) opts % relational = REL_LETTERS case ( 'keep' ) opts % relational = REL_KEEP case default call fail ( '\"symbols\", \"letters\" or \"keep\"' ) end select case default if ( index ( key , 'spaces.' ) == 1 ) then call set_spaces ( key ( 8 :)) else if ( index ( key , 'case.' ) == 1 ) then call set_case ( key ( 6 :)) else stat = 1 errmsg = 'unknown setting \"' // key // '\"' end if end select contains subroutine fail ( expected ) !! Report a bad value for the setting. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: expected !! description of the values allowed stat = 1 errmsg = 'expected ' // expected // ' for \"' // key // '\", not \"' // value // '\"' end subroutine fail subroutine read_count ( max_value , n ) !! Read the value as a whole number from 0 to `max_value` into `n`; `n` is unchanged if it is not one. integer , intent ( in ) :: max_value !! largest value allowed integer , intent ( inout ) :: n !! the option to set integer :: ios , v if ( verify ( value , '0123456789' ) == 0 . and . len ( value ) > 0 . and . len ( value ) <= 9 ) then read ( value , * , iostat = ios ) v if ( ios == 0 . and . v <= max_value ) then n = v return end if end if call fail ( 'a number from 0 to ' // to_s ( max_value )) end subroutine read_count subroutine read_flag ( flag ) !! Read the value, `true` or `false`, into `flag`; `flag` is unchanged if it is neither. logical , intent ( inout ) :: flag !! the option to set select case ( value ) case ( 'true' ) flag = . true . case ( 'false' ) flag = . false . case default call fail ( 'true or false' ) end select end subroutine read_flag subroutine set_spaces ( rule ) !! Set whitespace rule `rule` of `opts%spaces` (all rules for `all`) to the value: `add`, !! `remove` or `keep`. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: rule !! rule name, the key without `spaces.`, e.g. `comma` integer :: mode select case ( value ) case ( 'add' ) mode = WS_ADD case ( 'remove' ) mode = WS_REMOVE case ( 'keep' ) mode = WS_KEEP case default call fail ( 'add, remove or keep' ) return end select associate ( ws => opts % spaces ) select case ( rule ) case ( 'all' ) ws = whitespace_options_t ( mode , mode , mode , mode , mode , mode , mode , mode , mode , mode , mode , mode , & mode , mode , mode , mode ) case ( 'assignment' ) ws % assignment = mode case ( 'keyword-args' ) ws % keyword_args = mode case ( 'pointer' ) ws % pointer = mode case ( 'declarations' ) ws % declarations = mode case ( 'relational' ) ws % relational = mode case ( 'logical' ) ws % logical = mode case ( 'plus-minus' ) ws % plus_minus = mode case ( 'mult-div' ) ws % mult_div = mode case ( 'power' ) ws % power = mode case ( 'concat' ) ws % concat = mode case ( 'comma' ) ws % comma = mode case ( 'slice-colon' ) ws % slice_colon = mode case ( 'percent' ) ws % percent = mode case ( 'control-paren' ) ws % control_paren = mode case ( 'conditional' ) ws % conditional = mode case ( 'defined-operators' ) ws % defined_operators = mode case default stat = 1 errmsg = 'unknown whitespace rule \"' // rule // '\"' end select end associate end subroutine set_spaces subroutine set_case ( what ) !! Set the letter case of `what` in `opts%letter_case` to the value: `lower`, `upper` or `keep`. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: what !! `keywords`, `operators`, ... or `all`: the key without `case.` integer :: mode select case ( value ) case ( 'lower' ) mode = CASE_LOWER case ( 'upper' ) mode = CASE_UPPER case ( 'keep' ) mode = CASE_KEEP case default call fail ( 'lower, upper or keep' ) return end select select case ( what ) case ( 'all' ) opts % letter_case = case_options_t ( mode , mode , mode , mode , mode ) case ( 'keywords' ) opts % letter_case % keywords = mode case ( 'operators' ) opts % letter_case % operators = mode case ( 'procedures' ) opts % letter_case % procedures = mode case ( 'constants' ) opts % letter_case % constants = mode case ( 'types' ) opts % letter_case % types = mode case default stat = 1 errmsg = 'unknown case setting \"' // what // '\"' end select end subroutine set_case end subroutine apply_setting","tags":"","url":"proc/apply_setting.html"},{"title":"canonical_relational – fformat","text":"public pure function canonical_relational(text) result(t) The symbol spelling of a lowercase relational operator; other text is returned unchanged. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: text operator text, in lowercase Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Called by proc~~canonical_relational~~CalledByGraph proc~canonical_relational canonical_relational proc~code_signature code_signature proc~code_signature->proc~canonical_relational proc~same_token same_token proc~same_token->proc~canonical_relational proc~same_code same_code proc~same_code->proc~code_signature proc~same_code->proc~same_token Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure function canonical_relational ( text ) result ( t ) !! The symbol spelling of a lowercase relational operator; other text is returned unchanged. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: text !! operator text, in lowercase character ( len = :), allocatable :: t integer :: r 