operator written in `style` (`REL_SYMBOLS` or `REL_LETTERS`). character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: src !! source text integer , intent ( in ) :: style !! one of the REL_* constants; `REL_KEEP` returns `src` character ( len = :), allocatable :: out type ( source_t ) :: source type ( string_builder_t ) :: buf integer :: k , j , r if ( style == REL_KEEP ) then out = src return end if call parse_source ( src , source ) do k = 1 , source % stmts % n do j = source % stmts % s ( k )% first , source % stmts % s ( k )% last r = 0 if (. not . source % keep ( k ) . and . source % stmts % s ( k )% kind == SK_CODE ) r = operator_index ( j ) if ( r == 0 ) then call buf % append ( token_text ( src , source % tokens % tok ( j ))) else if ( style == REL_SYMBOLS ) then call buf % append ( trim ( SYMBOLS ( r ))) else call buf % append ( trim ( LETTERS ( r ))) end if end do end do out = buf % get () contains integer function operator_index ( j ) !! Index of token `j` in the operator tables, or 0 if it is not a relational operator. integer , intent ( in ) :: j !! index into the token list character ( len = :), allocatable :: t operator_index = 0 if ( source % tokens % tok ( j )% kind /= TK_OP . and . source % tokens % tok ( j )% kind /= TK_DOTOP ) return t = token_lower ( src , source % tokens % tok ( j )) if ( source % tokens % tok ( j )% kind == TK_OP ) then operator_index = findloc ( SYMBOLS , t , dim = 1 ) if ( is_chevron ( src , source % tokens , j )) operator_index = 0 else operator_index = findloc ( LETTERS , t , dim = 1 ) end if end function operator_index end function convert_relational","tags":"","url":"proc/convert_relational.html"},{"title":"is_use_statement – fformat","text":"public pure function is_use_statement(v) True if statement v is a use statement. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( statement_view_t ), intent(in) :: v the statement Return Value logical Called by proc~~is_use_statement~~CalledByGraph proc~is_use_statement is_use_statement proc~code