he\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code integer function directive ( src , t ) !! Formatter directive (one of the DIR_* constants) of a comment token. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: src !! source text type ( token_t ), intent ( in ) :: t !! a comment token of `src` character ( len = :), allocatable :: text integer :: n directive = DIR_NONE if ( t % sub /= CM_FORMATTER ) return text = token_text ( src , t ) n = len ( text ) do while ( n > 0 ) ! without trailing blanks and tabs if ( text ( n : n ) /= ' ' . and . text ( n : n ) /= achar ( 9 )) exit n = n - 1 end do text = text ( 1 : n ) if ( text == '!&<' ) then directive = DIR_OFF else if ( text == '!&>' ) then directive = DIR_ON else if ( len ( text ) == 2 ) then directive = DIR_KEEP else if ( text ( 3 : 3 ) == ' ' ) then directive = DIR_KEEP end if end function directive","tags":"","url":"proc/directive.html"},{"title":"protected_items – fformat","text":"public  function protected_items(src, tokens, stmts) result(keep) True for each item that must be written exactly as it is: statements with a !& comment, and\neverything from a !&< line to the next !&> line, both included. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: src source text type( token_list_t ), intent(in) :: tokens tokens of src type( statement_list_t ), intent(in) :: stmts items of tokens Return Value logical, allocatable, (:) Calls proc~~protected_items~~CallsGraph proc~protected_items protected_items proc~directive directive proc~protected_items->proc~directive proc~token_text token_text proc~directive->proc~token_text Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows poin