 survives), WS_REMOVE removes the blanks, and WS_KEEP leaves them as\nthey are. Rules only look at tokens on the same line; blanks are never added or removed next to a\nline break, a continuation & or a comment. Statements where operators have other meanings are recognized: unary + / - , * in real*8 , print * and (*) , / in array constructors, and in data , common , namelist , save and equivalence statements. format statements are left alone. Uses ffmt_tokens ffmt_statements ffmt_source ffmt_strings ffmt_options module~~ffmt_whitespace~~UsesGraph module~ffmt_whitespace ffmt_whitespace module~ffmt_options ffmt_options module~ffmt_whitespace->module~ffmt_options module~ffmt_source ffmt_source module~ffmt_whitespace->module~ffmt_source module~ffmt_statements ffmt_statements module~ffmt_whitespace->module~ffmt_statements module~ffmt_strings ffmt_strings module~ffmt_whitespace->module~ffmt_strings module~ffmt_tokens ffmt_tokens module~ffmt_whitespace->module~ffmt_tokens module~ffmt_source->module~ffmt_statements module~ffmt_source->module~ffmt_tokens module~ffmt_directives ffmt_directives module~ffmt_source->module~ffmt_directives module~ffmt_lexer ffmt_lexer module~ffmt_source->module~ffmt_lexer module~ffmt_statements->module~ffmt_strings module~ffmt_statements->module~ffmt_tokens module~ffmt_tokens->module~ffmt_strings module~ffmt_directives->module~ffmt_statements module~ffmt_directives->module~ffmt_tokens module~ffmt_lexer->module~ffmt_strings module~ffmt_lexer->module~ffmt_tokens Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~ffmt_whitespace~~UsedByGraph module~ffmt_whitespace ffmt_whitespace module~ffmt_format ffmt_format module~ffmt_f