","text":"Sorting use statements, and the names in their only: lists, alphabetically ignoring case. A group of use statements is a run of them with nothing between them: a blank line, comment,\npreprocessor line or any other statement ends the group, so statements in different #if branches never mix. A statement moves with its continuation lines and trailing comment.\nStatements that share a line with another ( ; ) or that are protected by formatter directives\nstay where they are and end the group. Statements of one group that use the same module keep\ntheir order. The names of an only: list are sorted by their local name ( c => x sorts as c ). A list that\nis not sorted yet is rewritten: on one line, for line splitting to break again, or broken at\ncommas to fit a given width, with its continuation lines starting below the first name. A\nstatement with a comment or preprocessor line before its last line is left alone. Uses ffmt_source ffmt_statements ffmt_strings ffmt_tokens module~~ffmt_use_sort~~UsesGraph module~ffmt_use_sort ffmt_use_sort module~ffmt_source ffmt_source module~ffmt_use_sort->module~ffmt_source module~ffmt_statements ffmt_statements module~ffmt_use_sort->module~ffmt_statements module~ffmt_strings ffmt_strings module~ffmt_use_sort->module~ffmt_strings module~ffmt_tokens ffmt_tokens module~ffmt_use_sort->module~ffmt_tokens module~ffmt_source->module~ffmt_statements module~ffmt_source->module~ffmt_tokens module~ffmt_directives ffmt_directives module~ffmt_source->module~ffmt_directives module~ffmt_lexer ffmt_lexer module~ffmt_source->module~ffmt_lexer module~ffmt_statements->module~ffmt_strings module~ffmt_statements->module~ffmt_tokens module~ffmt_tokens->module~ffmt_strings module~ffmt_directives->module~ffmt_statements module~ffmt_directives->module~ffmt_tokens module~ffmt_lexer->module~ffmt_strings module~ffmt_lexer->module~ffmt_tokens Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule S