anted between pairs of adjacent tokens. !! !! Each rule has a mode: `WS_ADD` makes sure there is at least one blank on each side (more are !! kept, so column alignment survives), `WS_REMOVE` removes the blanks, and `WS_KEEP` leaves them as !! they are. Rules only look at tokens on the same line; blanks are never added or removed next to a !! line break, a continuation `&` or a comment. !! !! Statements where operators have other meanings are recognized: unary `+`/`-`, `*` in `real*8`, !! `print *` and `(*)`, `/` in array constructors, and in `data`, `common`, `namelist`, `save` and !! `equivalence` statements. `format` statements are left alone. use ffmt_tokens use ffmt_statements use ffmt_options , only : whitespace_options_t , WS_ADD , WS_REMOVE use ffmt_source , only : source_t use ffmt_strings , only : utf8_width implicit none private public :: compute_gaps ! gaps: the blanks wanted before a token integer , parameter , public :: GAP_KEEP = - 1 !! as in the input integer , parameter , public :: GAP_MIN1 = - 2 !! at least one blank contains function compute_gaps ( source , views , ws , comment_spacing ) result ( gap ) !! The gap wanted before each token (`GAP_KEEP`, `GAP_MIN1` or a number of blanks). type ( source_t ), intent ( in ) :: source !! the source type ( statement_view_t ), intent ( in ) :: views (:) !! the view of each item (see [[statement_views]]) type ( whitespace_options_t ), intent ( in ) :: ws !! modes of the whitespace rules integer , intent ( in ) :: comment_spacing !! blanks before a trailing comment, or -1 to keep them integer , allocatable :: gap (:) integer :: k allocate ( gap ( source % tokens % n )) gap = GAP_KEEP do k = 1 , source % stmts % n if ( source % stmts % s ( k )% kind == SK_CODE ) call statement_gaps ( source % text , source % tokens , views ( k ), ws , gap ) end do if ( comment_spacing >= 0 ) call comment_gaps ( source , comment_spacing , gap ) end function compute_gaps subroutine comment_gaps ( source , spacing , gap ) !! Ask f